#{[{:activity/_scope [{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125406} :activity/id #uuid "9ba6f288-55b6-582e-8aa1-d15ec442bd9c" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125406 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125785 :tutorial/content "We can find the eigenvalues of a $3\\times 3$ matrix in much the same way as for $2\\!\\times\\! 2$ matrices. \n\nRemember, $\\lambda$ is an eigenvalue of $A$ if $A\\mathbf{v} = \\lambda\\mathbf{v}$ for some non-zero vector $\\mathbf{v}$. This implies that the equation\n\n$$\n(A-\\lambda I)\\mathbf{v}=\\mathbf{0}\n$$\n\nhas a non-trivial solution, which means that the matrix $A-\\lambda I$ is singular, and consequently\n$\\textrm{det}(A-\\lambda I)=0.$\nTherefore, if we want to find the eigenvalues of a $n\\!\\times\\! n$ matrix $A,$ we have to find the solutions of the characteristic equation\n\n$$\n\\textrm{det}(A-\\lambda I)=0.\n$$\n\nLet's go through this process in the case of the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n![](images/21/21e0994519fbba32a84020ce4661e98600c1307947083ddc3afe9902658143c1.svg)\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix $A-\\lambda I{:}$\n\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-\\lambda I & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\lambda \\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5-\\lambda \\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we set and solve the characteristic equation $\\,\\textrm{det}(A-\\lambda I)=0.$ Using the fact that the determinant of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix is given by the product of the elements on the main diagonal, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-2-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (-2-\\lambda )(-8-\\lambda )(5-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +2)(\\lambda +8)(\\lambda -5) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the eigenvalues of the matrix $A$ are $\\lambda=-2,$ $\\lambda=-8,$ and $\\lambda=5.$" :tutorial/id #uuid "535c5b8b-f815-5ded-8ae5-668bac420af7" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3564 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "9f05d37d-484a-5ae0-8ed9-0b46584f4a7f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125407}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125407 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124522 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "289ae874-f555-50ee-896f-eb2188004124"} :step/id #uuid "9edf1314-60a8-581e-afc3-f39ecd8b7951" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125408}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125408 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125786 :tutorial/content "The **algebraic multiplicity** of an eigenvalue $\\lambda$ is the number of times it is a solution of the characteristic equation. \n\nFor example, consider a $6\\times 6$ matrix $A$ with the following characteristic equation:\n\n$$\n(\\lambda-{\\color{red}4})(\\lambda-{\\color{red}4})(\\lambda-1)(\\lambda+8)^{\\color{blue}3} =0\n$$\n\nThe eigenvalue $\\lambda={\\color{red}4}$ is a double root. Therefore, it has algebraic multiplicity $2.$ \n\nBy the same reasoning, we say that \n\n- $\\lambda=1$ has algebraic multiplicity $1,$ and\n\n- $\\lambda=-8$ has algebraic multiplicity $\\color{blue}3$." :tutorial/id #uuid "db18f185-0dce-547f-95f2-71b60a6d4d2b" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3565 :tutorial/title "The Algebraic Multiplicity of an Eigenvalue"} :step/id #uuid "37883812-d28d-5bd5-97af-2df4b9f73f66" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125488}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125409 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124523 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5abea3ab-76a7-5598-8ede-b4cf88dd47d7"} :step/id #uuid "d8240de1-8637-5d84-886a-269d69011445"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125488 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124571 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef311af0-0e95-5574-a151-2971ad66bd08"} :step/id #uuid "1c9b6469-fe8d-5b75-bb95-efbf2684e9ce" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125409}}] :activity/title "The Characteristic Equation of a Matrix" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186124749} {:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442276} :activity/id #uuid "3b7302f6-4f44-5e74-82d2-2ea10325bde3" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442273 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272116 :question/id #uuid "29164807-d381-53a4-8efb-e16c83f907bf"} :step/id #uuid "3399fe8e-8176-5e35-93d5-9a34329ea9c3"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442274 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442271 :question/id #uuid "970b7afa-4ca1-5d4a-a4eb-b7279227d558"} :step/id #uuid "34fc937b-c4ca-51d0-b41f-cc48a4e031b8" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442277}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442275 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442272 :question/id #uuid "bedee111-5fec-56ad-a271-6904f3e057b2"} :step/id #uuid "41fe8de5-4b38-5378-88a7-29da8122c672" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442273}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442276 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125062 :question/id #uuid "c699a77c-6393-5572-b010-6743d9f3bb17"} :step/id #uuid "4407ab4d-760d-5929-a4aa-ceca8bb19594" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442274}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442277 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323910 :question/id #uuid "4b421cae-1cc2-5e38-a509-6349aee206e1"} :step/id #uuid "e50043bb-5fa2-5c1d-b766-cd5b3092a18e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442275}}] :activity/title "The Characteristic Equation of a Matrix" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442258} {:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492085} :activity/id #uuid "bb1cab8e-f559-528e-91c4-523487085390" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492076 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492037 :question/id #uuid "92a47338-e5c2-507b-a67f-16316e526b27"} :step/id #uuid "09549905-c795-54bf-8c12-03fa23a953b9" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492106}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492085 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125013 :question/id #uuid "f39262c6-06ce-51e6-92a2-5f2acfb813a4"} :step/id #uuid "2d974ac8-4b52-5e20-b579-6e1ce93781a6" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492087}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492087 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442271 :question/id #uuid "970b7afa-4ca1-5d4a-a4eb-b7279227d558"} :step/id #uuid "340f24d2-fb9b-5c2f-b6ce-923f20f3fce5" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492076}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492099 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272102 :question/id #uuid "61624282-afa1-5aa5-87a3-f50541d7253a"} :step/id #uuid "95cae298-e2af-5367-a5a3-02954c8d6de6"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492106 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366518 :question/id #uuid "09a3b9db-e65e-598f-9745-d20fbdbcba69"} :step/id #uuid "c5e318ec-24f1-53a2-b4da-1e201af09eaa" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492099}}] :activity/title "The Characteristic Equation of a Matrix" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491446}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186050376 :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124522 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124331 :question/id #uuid "4b2fcf5d-0da3-5676-b4c6-54095c3fb45c" :question/math-academy-id "e-5486" :question/problem "Determine all real eigenvalues $\\lambda$ of the matrix \n![](images/45/4549ab32dddcf46e297a3238d71a51657bbcf5fa1c4b2659000c023fff6f938d.svg)" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\, A-\\lambda I \\mathbin{:}$\n﻿﻿﻿![](images/99/99bf36b6acbdd21ab16ca6b434122fed7c474103f6e88ec5688261d5848d542c.svg)\n\nThe characteristic equation is $\\det(A-\\lambda I) = 0.$ \n\nSince the determinant of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix is given by the product of the entries on the main diagonal, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-9-\\lambda  & 4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 9-\\lambda  & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-9-\\lambda )(9-\\lambda )(6-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +9)(\\lambda -9)(\\lambda -6) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda_1=-9,$ $\\lambda_2=9,$ and $\\lambda_3=6.$ \n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are always the entries on the main diagonal."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "289ae874-f555-50ee-896f-eb2188004124" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125012 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a22ae914-eefb-5975-9b0f-5a27d28c6132" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "λ ∈ {-2, 3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122673} {:answer/id #uuid "c08eba2a-5e5a-5380-979b-32db6ac0cb46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "λ ∈ {-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122674} {:answer/id #uuid "cca08244-779e-521a-99c1-161f55a3ce64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "λ ∈ {-2,-1, 4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122675} {:answer/id #uuid "201219c0-0f24-5f90-a03f-c05a1c2872d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "λ ∈ {-2, 3, 4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122676} {:answer/id #uuid "642c8c67-ace8-5bc1-adb5-d88f862d0b79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "λ ∈ {-4,-2, 3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122677}] :answer-field/id #uuid "8e3898e9-8787-559d-a597-4830d4990984" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122672}] :question/id #uuid "a451407b-df1a-5469-850d-9d3e8b92e100" :question/math-academy-id "q-36822" :question/problem "Determine all real eigenvalues $λ$ of the matrix\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125017 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34b63fae-2f7c-5fe2-a1a4-0ec3c381a3dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda -4)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321550} {:answer/id #uuid "7e0eb44e-ac21-5b2a-a972-1f77bba194b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda +4)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322140} {:answer/id #uuid "9bb97b3b-8054-574a-8ea2-ed4ef42cb19d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda -10)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322378} {:answer/id #uuid "d58e6bae-778a-5650-bdd1-f71c17fa7409" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda -16)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322813} {:answer/id #uuid "d90d6023-7a0f-5e73-af24-24eac2a1b5b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-16)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322849}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda -16)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322813} :answer-field/id #uuid "55997a27-4ab4-5568-9f4a-ccc1b73a2faf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323333}] :question/id #uuid "2accab64-f6f1-5300-b0aa-a3471aee3ef9" :question/math-academy-id "q-36845" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=\\begin{bmatrix}-3-\\lambda  & 2 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 2-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(A-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $3$rd row, we obtain the following:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-3-\\lambda  & 2 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 2-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )\\begin{vmatrix}-3-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 5 & 2-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )((-3-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda )-2\\cdot 5) & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda -16) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323857 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16474b71-dd87-5c02-90a1-1986cdcc2b44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +3)(\\lambda -2)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321329} {:answer/id #uuid "455b312d-436f-5a59-beed-3c43b768e4a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +1)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321696} {:answer/id #uuid "9521fe4a-7fce-5da7-a5cc-1b5de6565706" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda (\\lambda -2)(\\lambda +2)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322336} {:answer/id #uuid "9e18c66c-1798-5646-b90c-5aa3dcdc792b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda +3)(\\lambda -2)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322392} {:answer/id #uuid "eb00f264-ac0e-52cf-bbb6-b0d74f11988e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -1)(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -2)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322987}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda +3)(\\lambda -2)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322392} :answer-field/id #uuid "05b0b363-ceb3-501c-b8ad-22246e96a7de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323175}] :question/id #uuid "a91b44ac-1def-566a-a0ac-b4f797a0bab1" :question/math-academy-id "q-36860" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=\\begin{bmatrix}-2-\\lambda  & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1-\\lambda  & -1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(A-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $2$nd column, we obtain the following:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-2-\\lambda  & 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1-\\lambda  & -1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (-1-\\lambda )\\begin{vmatrix}-2-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (-1-\\lambda )((-2-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )-(-2)(-2)) & =0 \\\\ (-1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda -6) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)(\\lambda +3)(\\lambda -2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323904 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c03b0d6-311f-55a2-81e5-71e742dd7ac5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -2)({\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +10)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321359} {:answer/id #uuid "1c6d5a60-4a1c-585b-9c6a-c38aad8c908f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda +3)(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda -3)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321363} {:answer/id #uuid "865a1300-13a1-5889-ab1b-b6361dc737c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -1)^{2}(\\lambda +2)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322214} {:answer/id #uuid "92792d5d-eeb6-5848-b334-bcfc0d1701dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda +2)({\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda -10)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322309} {:answer/id #uuid "a6d6efdd-902a-5ff9-acb4-e7d10dff1a1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda +2)({\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +10)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322452}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda +2)({\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +10)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322452} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a26514d-bab5-54f6-affd-0baea61f5deb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323220}] :question/id #uuid "a0e8e60c-423d-5778-945d-945b43ca8811" :question/math-academy-id "q-37354" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,B-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nB-\\lambda I=\\begin{bmatrix}1-\\lambda  & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -3 & 5 & 1-\\lambda \\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(B-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $2$nd row, we obtain the following:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}1-\\lambda  & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -3 & 5 & 1-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (-2-\\lambda )\\begin{vmatrix}1-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ -3 & 1-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (-2-\\lambda )((1-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )-(3)(-3)) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +2)({\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +10) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323909 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ec2a17b-686d-53a5-85bd-9f9a7c05b248" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda +3)(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +2)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321262} {:answer/id #uuid "4436935a-9c77-5825-93ad-4fe1440b7256" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -8)(\\lambda +7)(\\lambda -3)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321685} {:answer/id #uuid "74b1c2e5-6145-5cc4-bc94-aaebe4115544" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda (\\lambda -6)(\\lambda +7)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322057} {:answer/id #uuid "9463a6bd-6039-5bb1-b51a-8f0a65ed10b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +2)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322326} {:answer/id #uuid "de933d31-9237-5767-9e80-05ad65f12e20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -6)(\\lambda +1)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322886}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +2)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322326} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0111eb3-d3cf-5281-ab8a-9aad7c4b0933" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323511}] :question/id #uuid "85bd5d94-8ec9-55aa-af68-90409443e4f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-37390" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 10 & 0 \\\\ -5 & -7 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -9 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,B-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nB-\\lambda I=\\begin{bmatrix}8-\\lambda  & 10 & 0 \\\\ -5 & -7-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 6 & -9 & 3-\\lambda \\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(B-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $3$rd column, we obtain the following:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}8-\\lambda  & 10 & 0 \\\\ -5 & -7-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 6 & -9 & 3-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )\\begin{vmatrix}8-\\lambda  & 10 \\\\ -5 & -7-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )((8-\\lambda )(-7-\\lambda )-(-5)(10)) & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -6) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400881 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c340906-07d4-57b0-9046-295287f1840f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in {3,0,6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400883} {:answer/id #uuid "735c9554-2122-554a-9c6d-88f5c542af17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in {3,4,9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400884} {:answer/id #uuid "cf676211-b439-541c-a870-387de50e341e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in {3,-2,6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400885} {:answer/id #uuid "5f97e983-0e63-57dd-acda-842c7a7cfb12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in {3,4,6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400886} {:answer/id #uuid "812db70d-b4af-5153-8bf4-a315c5a42142" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in {-3,4,6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400887}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in {3,4,6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400886} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ed14d3f-a85e-59d0-a5e0-cd86b0195649" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186400882}] :question/id #uuid "f772a19b-8ab2-5f26-9ef1-47231e01914d" :question/math-academy-id "q-140449" :question/problem "Determine all real eigenvalues $\\lambda $ of the matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 3 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=\\begin{bmatrix}4-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 3-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 6-\\lambda \\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(A-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nSince the determinant of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix is given by the product of the entries on the main diagonal, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}4-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 3-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 6-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )(3-\\lambda )(6-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -6) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}=3,$ $\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=4,$ and ${\\lambda }_{3}=6.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are always the entries on the main diagonal."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427385 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fde5085-a635-5696-9cd7-100b3c72cad2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-1,4,1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427374} {:answer/id #uuid "578c36b5-c09b-5821-8e36-ba81ab9528bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-1,-4,1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427376} {:answer/id #uuid "78e32da7-f1e3-50b7-a080-2498d2b37830" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{2,0,1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427377} {:answer/id #uuid "cfdc823e-90d7-5645-a8fc-5def08fa694a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{2,4,0\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427381} {:answer/id #uuid "ed7b9e7c-c2fe-5559-be97-bb8125d6fa51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-1,2,0\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427382}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-1,4,1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427374} :answer-field/id #uuid "0da5b7ce-3185-5f7f-9a0f-797454d122c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427384}] :question/id #uuid "2ffb7e93-f33c-5adf-acf0-f55e6fbbb059" :question/math-academy-id "q-36831" :question/problem "Determine all real eigenvalues $\\lambda $ of the matrix \n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,B-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nB-\\lambda I=\\begin{bmatrix}-1-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(B-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nSince the determinant of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix is given by the product of the entries on the main diagonal, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-1-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (-1-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-1,$ $\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=4,$ and ${\\lambda }_{3}=1.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are always the entries on the main diagonal."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447470 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "527cb312-c6a6-5a5d-9bcf-61787139c3d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda (\\lambda +10)(\\lambda -20)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447402} {:answer/id #uuid "6561688f-0f5b-5532-a636-4e1b1e285d0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda +40)(\\lambda -6)(\\lambda -30)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447408} {:answer/id #uuid "6e034595-10dd-5a5a-8870-372a9c9d5b27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}(\\lambda +10)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447412} {:answer/id #uuid "beaaed4b-e3bf-59ab-9162-b63b3f77485b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -10)(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda +20)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447436} {:answer/id #uuid "d221a7d6-bd60-5f61-a4eb-8f48bc286186" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda +80)(\\lambda -14)(\\lambda -60)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447440}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda (\\lambda +10)(\\lambda -20)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447402} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4136c8d-5a3d-54a3-8e0e-9880d33a4256" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447459}] :question/id #uuid "a82c548a-99d5-5982-b67f-c8bf62fc70fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-37357" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}-40 & 6 & 30 \\\\ 0 & -10 & 0 \\\\ -80 & 14 & 60\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,B-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nB-\\lambda I=\\begin{bmatrix}-40-\\lambda  & 6 & 30 \\\\ 0 & -10-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -80 & 14 & 60-\\lambda \\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(B-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $2$nd row, we obtain the following:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-40-\\lambda  & 6 & 30 \\\\ 0 & -10-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -80 & 14 & 60-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (-10-\\lambda )\\begin{vmatrix}-40-\\lambda  & 30 \\\\ -80 & 60-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (-10-\\lambda )((-40-\\lambda )(60-\\lambda )-(30)(-80)) & =0 \\\\ (-10-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-20\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +10)(\\lambda )(\\lambda -20) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda +10)(\\lambda -20) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447472 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0dd806b5-b00a-5419-b12d-acd06881a066" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{3,4,-5\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447379} {:answer/id #uuid "81325892-1923-5229-ade2-a096f5c023d6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-3,0,3\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447420} {:answer/id #uuid "8d939250-f6e6-5ac0-9745-e9c2d7ddd5e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-3,-4,5\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447424} {:answer/id #uuid "978f7fe8-15da-52c6-ba65-b60baa2efb75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{0,-4,-2\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447427} {:answer/id #uuid "c32cb1b1-29a5-5579-8622-98540b8194df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-3,-2,5\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447437}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-3,-4,5\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447424} :answer-field/id #uuid "b75011bd-dfba-5826-af46-a8b32028e02b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447460}] :question/id #uuid "bca3e3e8-22f6-5c69-8cd2-18d06e6e998f" :question/math-academy-id "q-80553" :question/problem "Determine all real eigenvalues $\\lambda $ of the matrix \n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,B-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nB-\\lambda I=\\begin{bmatrix}-3-\\lambda  & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -4-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5-\\lambda \\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(B-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nSince the determinant of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix is given by the product of the entries on the main diagonal, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-3-\\lambda  & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -4-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (-3-\\lambda )(-4-\\lambda )(5-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +3)(\\lambda +4)(\\lambda -5) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-3,$ $\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-4,$ and ${\\lambda }_{3}=5.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are always the entries on the main diagonal."}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a 3x3 Matrix Containing a Block of Zeros"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124523 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124332 :question/id #uuid "76c52a74-9b98-5df5-ac63-64e92af1a580" :question/math-academy-id "e-5487" :question/problem "Determine all real eigenvalues ![](images/98/98a445be63a324ba80515c96b7f891797392bdeafb375acb75ce1613f4475d4c.svg) of the matrix \n![](images/f1/f1bc09a8e52ccd286aa0e28fee7f60b17b48ce7423eb897269ab9fda387a93dc.svg)" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix ![](images/da/da1b043be21ae49536ac74a7c5df40af321f327b25fce325a54d87bca7bdd804.svg)\n﻿﻿﻿![](images/0c/0ced5cb154bbec90b1d0832ac1e2bf9e0b3599d4675784a47b32f69861b63549.svg)\n\nThe characteristic equation is given by ![](images/7d/7db7ee38ff2ad420ad85266b4684a9092ca4976b0a312043cdcb40f755f87312.svg) \n\nExpanding the determinant across the ![](images/95/95836ae470c61ab15bfb67d6f0c92d2ad8d03d400b04473e81e58de3ee44bf32.svg)st row, we get the following:\n\n![](images/8a/8a07ee34efc93d9c0454d7275b94f5dcd303a938784b797a265eba29356f5801.svg)\n\nNow, we need to solve this equation. We find the first root by testing some values. According to the rational zeros theorem, a list of good first guesses consists of all divisors of ![](images/22/225eed5110c60c0ca4c2205a24ba280024533de3e65ad4d32fae9617ce06b4a9.svg) \n![](images/04/04cd74c64ddaedf3b73761d8098979ac86cd9089751a10278b9aedd2bc8f98dc.svg)\n\nLet's pick ![](images/96/9656fb92a4f17a34456f345565f0e7d85fd432d9cd38070cdada71e52647529c.svg) Substituting to the characteristic equation gives\n![](images/5d/5d2e25abee3cc05da3b3a83482899c4b6558fd54a4d66e39331ba1b55f50a917.svg)\nSo, ![](images/0a/0a68ef90ceec4971dc74a1a73e0a5bbdee3eec5956ddbce404a48517b2828059.svg) is a root of the equation. This means we can factor ![](images/ff/ffad613e6c3731c1406a83b447c4212d48bc41005ca7817a73d5c2ed66f79b30.svg) out of ![](images/03/0367fad967f1c2089ceaefb337b32b0a39b425dd3f0f900ec7b859547a036a89.svg) using synthetic division:\n\n| ![](images/95/95836ae470c61ab15bfb67d6f0c92d2ad8d03d400b04473e81e58de3ee44bf32.svg) | ![](images/95/95836ae470c61ab15bfb67d6f0c92d2ad8d03d400b04473e81e58de3ee44bf32.svg) | ![](images/0c/0cf2eee0cdec31b7acdc244a255aaee7d6d520cfeee67b64ac9cf215f5377477.svg) | ![](images/f1/f1557a7d98a910797c6117a185f64b753b0ebcd56db3f187aca1952f4f38df5c.svg) | ![](images/8e/8ec9094ad8c9b7c6e3da424099eca8e856a690c4355d4af8210da28f495a72f0.svg) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | ![](images/11/113a2e06675ede52bfef4b9178bf4e7820332c07c597cb963b36a5bbef55f6cf.svg) | ![](images/95/95836ae470c61ab15bfb67d6f0c92d2ad8d03d400b04473e81e58de3ee44bf32.svg) | ![](images/37/37e17c4a2302e6352fb7186621c9c43bb5e99d43a8a0bc700c0181d36c6cc915.svg) | ![](images/46/46908fb7561d19927fe58a38ab26cba3ff8a35cf75cc0da234f08773dc991398.svg) |\n|  | ![](images/95/95836ae470c61ab15bfb67d6f0c92d2ad8d03d400b04473e81e58de3ee44bf32.svg) | ![](images/37/37e17c4a2302e6352fb7186621c9c43bb5e99d43a8a0bc700c0181d36c6cc915.svg) | ![](images/46/46908fb7561d19927fe58a38ab26cba3ff8a35cf75cc0da234f08773dc991398.svg) | ![](images/15/156b31ede73de5301befe67f02745a0202f1806a62f9fdecc6fc9ee3f21117ba.svg) |\n\nSo, we obtain the following factorization:\n![](images/d8/d802c5d6ff81a500a8d7d00ec9e20daafb07d355a1ce0d9a0b48dc03a88088c9.svg)\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are ![](images/19/191f231d4e62c28931ed18cf133acb0e0ec66e845af743409198c4420953bd52.svg) ![](images/eb/eb3981cb149c9d1b26c2b87bd92a5aef5ead1787d8cb817fa3c1efd6a66074f9.svg) and ![](images/e9/e988f1ab98136f2d888e83baf436d8f659654a55eb2d2b3e11029b365a52c6e0.svg)"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5abea3ab-76a7-5598-8ede-b4cf88dd47d7" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125013 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2dc50313-1349-57e5-bd5b-c32ef21846c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5{\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda -4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427375} {:answer/id #uuid "ba3bf449-9417-55d8-bda3-bcdf2a3abb0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}+2{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -2=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427378} {:answer/id #uuid "bb4847f7-518c-5520-9f7b-8f055c77b9d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}-5{\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda =0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427379} {:answer/id #uuid "c9d9c2bc-05e4-5243-ab8a-17562b551bd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}-5{\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda -2=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427380} {:answer/id #uuid "f431214a-fe2c-58fb-acc6-9d70412cfbb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}-2\\lambda -2=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427383}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}+2{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -2=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427378} :answer-field/id #uuid "b55f74a2-418f-5fce-b67f-29118bc0950f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122678}] :question/id #uuid "f39262c6-06ce-51e6-92a2-5f2acfb813a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-36824" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -5\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\lambda  & -2 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 3-\\lambda  & 6 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -5-\\lambda \\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(A-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $1$st row, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-\\lambda  & -2 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 3-\\lambda  & 6 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -5-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ -\\lambda \\begin{vmatrix}3-\\lambda  & 6 \\\\ -2 & -5-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix}-(-2)\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -5-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix}+(-3)\\begin{vmatrix}-2 & 3-\\lambda  \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ -\\lambda ({\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda -3)+2(2\\lambda -2)-3(2\\lambda -2) & =0 \\\\ (-{\\lambda }^{3}-2{\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda )+(4\\lambda -4)-(6\\lambda -6) & =0 \\\\ -{\\lambda }^{3}-2{\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda +2 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{3}+2{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -2 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125016 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b850092-0768-5d13-a72a-e11e6fa61527" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "λ ∈ {1, 2, 3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122697} {:answer/id #uuid "f3a1a73f-8bf5-5f94-b424-b7f3670c257a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "λ ∈ {2, 3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122698} {:answer/id #uuid "092448a6-840b-51dc-a7ec-b41d39ae8c3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "λ ∈ {-5,-1, 2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122699} {:answer/id #uuid "137b35b1-2635-5ab0-a9bf-0aed4b658b9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "λ ∈ {1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122700} {:answer/id #uuid "28788f1a-eb82-5d27-8d2e-99d46877bcae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "λ ∈ {-3, 1, 2}" :db/id #edb/ref 175921