lambda }^{3}+4{\\lambda }^{2}-53\\lambda -36=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321174} {:answer/id #uuid "1d8b6827-a8f5-5e9e-a456-3c1f4b0bd806" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}+4{\\lambda }^{2}-37\\lambda -108=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321371} {:answer/id #uuid "53cbf2a7-4b85-5a35-aa42-5f47e5014747" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}-4{\\lambda }^{2}-37\\lambda +72=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321806} {:answer/id #uuid "5844cdec-8e7d-5d66-a293-f8b40e411e1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}+4{\\lambda }^{2}-37\\lambda -72=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321840} {:answer/id #uuid "ac8c4ccf-02d4-5b71-8706-613880e25eb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}-4{\\lambda }^{2}+53\\lambda +36=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322498}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}+4{\\lambda }^{2}-37\\lambda -72=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321840} :answer-field/id #uuid "11bd07c2-d426-5569-a039-db8a048a82ba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323203}] :question/id #uuid "04cda9cf-e19f-5987-86a4-1bd75a963670" :question/math-academy-id "q-37396" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & -8 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,B-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nB-\\lambda I=\\begin{bmatrix}-9-\\lambda  & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5-\\lambda  & -8 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -\\lambda \\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(B-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $1$st row, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-9-\\lambda  & 9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5-\\lambda  & -8 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (-9-\\lambda )\\begin{vmatrix}5-\\lambda  & -8 \\\\ 1 & -\\lambda \\end{vmatrix}-9\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -8 \\\\ -2 & -\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (-9-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +8)-9(-16) & =0 \\\\ (-{\\lambda }^{3}-4{\\lambda }^{2}+37\\lambda -72)+144 & =0 \\\\ -{\\lambda }^{3}-4{\\lambda }^{2}+37\\lambda +72 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{3}+4{\\lambda }^{2}-37\\lambda -72 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366013 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fd702e4-330a-55c4-a31c-c235740df973" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}-2{\\lambda }^{2}-109\\lambda +470=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366015} {:answer/id #uuid "1bc53b3d-fa24-5966-986f-e002765bf747" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}-2{\\lambda }^{2}-31\\lambda +32=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366016} {:answer/id #uuid "7fb400bf-02c7-5b7d-be66-3597e2682ca1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}+2{\\lambda }^{2}-10\\lambda -5=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366017} {:answer/id #uuid "d4b97459-5f9c-583d-bbf4-79230e9fff2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}-2{\\lambda }^{2}-109\\lambda +110=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366018} {:answer/id #uuid "4587a64e-a88f-55cb-a42a-0f3b6f625361" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}-2{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda +2=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366019}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}-2{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda +2=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366019} :answer-field/id #uuid "23f37a83-a62e-50f1-affa-75b650e2059a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366014}] :question/id #uuid "94bfabe8-f33f-5580-888f-0bac595dc86b" :question/math-academy-id "q-37395" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$C=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 & -6 \\\\ 4 & 5 & -12 \\\\ 3 & 3 & -7\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,C-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nC-\\lambda I=\\begin{bmatrix}4-\\lambda  & 3 & -6 \\\\ 4 & 5-\\lambda  & -12 \\\\ 3 & 3 & -7-\\lambda \\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(C-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $1$st row, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}4-\\lambda  & 3 & -6 \\\\ 4 & 5-\\lambda  & -12 \\\\ 3 & 3 & -7-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )\\begin{vmatrix}5-\\lambda  & -12 \\\\ 3 & -7-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix}-3\\begin{vmatrix}4 & -12 \\\\ 3 & -7-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix}+(-6)\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 5-\\lambda  \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +1)-3(-4\\lambda +8)-6(-3+3\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (-{\\lambda }^{3}+2{\\lambda }^{2}+7\\lambda +4)-(-12\\lambda +24)-(-18+18\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ -{\\lambda }^{3}+2{\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda -2 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{3}-2{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda +2 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366518 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5fb7b1df-59af-5c98-b200-8e2db9ace225" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}-3{\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda -10=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366520} {:answer/id #uuid "780e1a23-2b19-569c-80de-ba05aa572a33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}-4{\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda -6=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366521} {:answer/id #uuid "1e23239c-8a66-52b7-8ebb-bb679392ff42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}+4{\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda +10=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366522} {:answer/id #uuid "d9d592de-a8e2-59d7-af6e-a3bf5bfd67b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}-3{\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda -6=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366523} {:answer/id #uuid "023efe6a-1a85-50a5-b630-83708ee21893" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}-4{\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda -10=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366524}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}-4{\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda -10=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366524} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a1a646e-8c46-51ec-bc79-a886445b9b9d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366519}] :question/id #uuid "09a3b9db-e65e-598f-9745-d20fbdbcba69" :question/math-academy-id "q-86753" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$R=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,R-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nR-\\lambda I=\\begin{bmatrix}1-\\lambda  & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3-\\lambda \\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(R-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $1$st column, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(R-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}1-\\lambda  & 2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )\\begin{vmatrix}-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ 1 & 3-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix}-(-2)\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-3\\lambda -4)+2(-2\\lambda +7) & =0 \\\\ (-{\\lambda }^{3}+4{\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda -4)+(-4\\lambda +14) & =0 \\\\ -{\\lambda }^{3}+4{\\lambda }^{2}-3\\lambda +10 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{3}-4{\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda -10 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186404128 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35af3a4a-7335-5fe9-967e-58adf4f90f66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-1,2\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447393} {:answer/id #uuid "5224fac3-9456-54c5-8164-7b956ad4457d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-1,2,-3\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447401} {:answer/id #uuid "583a945a-8104-5e57-8cc3-097d8e920823" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{1,-6\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447404} {:answer/id #uuid "bda8e9d4-016c-519c-908c-da427a5c28c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-1,-2,3\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447434} {:answer/id #uuid "be3f9e84-b89f-56ff-858a-b9716e9565bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{2,-3\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447435}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-1,-2,3\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447434} :answer-field/id #uuid "135ac5a3-acd1-57d7-85af-ac59d7bb8214" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404129}] :question/id #uuid "ba3b9cc6-841d-5636-9777-0bc1e8c24e7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-80825" :question/problem "Determine all real eigenvalues $\\lambda $ of the matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=\\begin{bmatrix}-1-\\lambda  & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -1-\\lambda \\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is given by $det(A-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $1$st row, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-1-\\lambda  & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -1-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (-1-\\lambda )\\begin{vmatrix}2-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix}-1\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (-{\\lambda }^{3}+6\\lambda +5)-(-1-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ -{\\lambda }^{3}+7\\lambda +6 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{3}-7\\lambda -6 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to solve this equation. We find the first root by testing some values. According to the rational zeros theorem, a list of good first guesses consists of all divisors of $6:$ \n\n$$\n\\pm 1,\\pm 2,\\pm 3,\\pm 6\n$$\n\n- Let's pick $x=1.$ Substituting to the characteristic equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1)^{3}-7(1)-6 & =-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $\\lambda =1$ is not a root of the equation.\n\n- Let's pick $x=-1.$ Substituting to the characteristic equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1)^{3}-7(-1)-6 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $\\lambda =-1$ is a root of the equation.\n\nSo, we can factor $(\\lambda +1)$ out of ${\\lambda }^{3}-7\\lambda -6$ using synthetic division:\n\n| $-1$ | $1$ | $0$ | $-7$ | $-6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $↓$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $6$ |\n|  | $1$ | $-1$ | $-6$ | $0$ |\n\nSo, we obtain the following factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda +1)({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -6) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda -3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-1,$ $\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-2,\\,$ and $\\,{\\lambda }_{3}=3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186404378 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19327b5d-0a87-5236-be0f-a4fc408fd3c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in {-2,-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404380} {:answer/id #uuid "576f8439-f4e9-50c2-87d9-f9f73bc72cf2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in {-2,1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404381} {:answer/id #uuid "b2e67c97-48f5-50c6-a340-ea3827974147" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in {-1,1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404382} {:answer/id #uuid "f6484944-66bf-551b-bebc-dde27bbefb01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in {-2,-1,1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404383} {:answer/id #uuid "e2d3b84a-b250-5e99-b0bf-b2e2d4abe21c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in {2,-1,1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404384}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in {-2,-1,1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404383} :answer-field/id #uuid "e326b9f3-50f4-5bf4-9fe5-a7fbee316948" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404379}] :question/id #uuid "8b75d1ac-303a-511c-86a2-e86c1eaa7201" :question/math-academy-id "q-86758" :question/problem "Determine all real eigenvalues $\\lambda $ of the matrix \n$O=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,O-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nO-\\lambda I=\\begin{bmatrix}-1-\\lambda  & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -\\lambda \\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is given by $det(O-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $1$st row, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(O-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-1-\\lambda  & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (-1-\\lambda )\\begin{vmatrix}-1-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 1 & -\\lambda \\end{vmatrix}+1\\begin{vmatrix}0 & -1-\\lambda  \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (-{\\lambda }^{3}-2{\\lambda }^{2}+1)+(\\lambda +1) & =0 \\\\ -{\\lambda }^{3}-2{\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda +2 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{3}+2{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -2 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to solve this equation. We find the first root by testing some values. According to the rational zeros theorem, a list of good first guesses consists of all divisors of $2:$ \n\n$$\n\\pm 1,\\pm 2\n$$\n\nLet's pick $x=1.$ Substituting to the characteristic equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1)^{3}+2(1)^{2}-(1)-2 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $\\lambda =1$ is a root of the equation. So, we can factor $(\\lambda -1)$ out of ${\\lambda }^{3}+2{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -2$ using synthetic division:\n\n| $1$ | $1$ | $2$ | $-1$ | $-2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $↓$ | $1$ | $3$ | $2$ |\n|  | $1$ | $3$ | $2$ | $0$ |\n\nSo, we obtain the following factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda -1)({\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda +2) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda +1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}=1,$ $\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-2,\\,$ and $\\,{\\lambda }_{3}=-1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442272 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d0700ae-412d-51b3-a257-618c99674341" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-2,1,5\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442260} {:answer/id #uuid "481860b5-bb3d-58cb-94dc-529c4d401e99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-5,1,3\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442261} {:answer/id #uuid "558359c6-2d82-546e-a690-6c2a868d98cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{1,2,5\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442262} {:answer/id #uuid "6819477a-eb82-5fe8-9144-a2c3b8ccd8c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-5,-1,2\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442263} {:answer/id #uuid "974ccec8-a09e-54db-b466-a20773981b7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-5,1,2\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442266}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-5,1,2\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442266} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8e6f41c-9e5c-55de-9517-8eaa2b14ab20" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442270}] :question/id #uuid "bedee111-5fec-56ad-a271-6904f3e057b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-140475" :question/problem "Determine all real eigenvalues $\\lambda $ of the matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=\\begin{bmatrix}3-\\lambda  & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -2-\\lambda \\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is given by $det(A-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $1$st row, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}3-\\lambda  & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -2-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )\\begin{vmatrix}-3-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ 2 & -2-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix}-(-1)\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix}+(-1)\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -3-\\lambda  \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (-{\\lambda }^{3}-2{\\lambda }^{2}+15\\lambda )+(-5-\\lambda )+(5+\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ -{\\lambda }^{3}-2{\\lambda }^{2}+13\\lambda -10 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{3}+2{\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda +10 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to solve this equation. We find the first root by testing some values. According to the rational zeros theorem, a list of good first guesses consists of all divisors of $10:$ \n\n$$\n\\pm 1,\\pm 2,\\pm 5,\\pm 10\n$$\n\nLet's pick $x=1.$ Substituting to the characteristic equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1)^{3}+2(1)^{2}-13(1)+10 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $\\lambda =1$ is a root of the equation. So, we can factor $(\\lambda -1)$ out of ${\\lambda }^{3}+2{\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda +10$ using synthetic division:\n\n| $1$ | $1$ | $2$ | $-13$ | $10$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $↓$ | $1$ | $3$ | $-10$ |\n|  | $1$ | $3$ | $-10$ | $0$ |\n\nSo, we obtain the following factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda -1)({\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda -10) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +5)(\\lambda -2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-5,$ $\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=1,\\,$ and $\\,{\\lambda }_{3}=2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492037 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15237b61-8e4a-5f9d-a46d-f1c679f25f0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-1,-2,4\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491497} {:answer/id #uuid "b7d351e3-6f87-5e60-9b75-e0173bdd7a1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-1,1,-8\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491771} {:answer/id #uuid "cd09c6e2-8436-5664-8cd9-04b180376a9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{1,8\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491802} {:answer/id #uuid "efa5985d-1ed5-5b85-9d5e-b97611697302" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-1,2,4\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491864} {:answer/id #uuid "f7df2b21-bb30-525d-9e2e-3424c69767ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-1,8\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491878}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-1,8\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491878} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b06b2ac-6eae-593d-9852-5522b16478ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491913}] :question/id #uuid "92a47338-e5c2-507b-a67f-16316e526b27" :question/math-academy-id "q-80821" :question/problem "Determine all real eigenvalues $\\lambda $ of the matrix \n$P=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,P-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nP-\\lambda I=\\begin{bmatrix}3-\\lambda  & 2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 3-\\lambda \\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is given by $det(P-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $1$st row, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}3-\\lambda  & 2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 3-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )\\begin{vmatrix}-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix}-2\\begin{vmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix}+4\\begin{vmatrix}2 & -\\lambda  \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (-{\\lambda }^{3}+6{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda -12)-2(-2-2\\lambda )+4(4+4\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ -{\\lambda }^{3}+6{\\lambda }^{2}+15\\lambda +8 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{3}-6{\\lambda }^{2}-15\\lambda -8 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to solve this equation. We find the first root by testing some values. According to the rational zeros theorem, a list of good first guesses consists of all divisors of $8:$ \n\n$$\n\\pm 1,\\pm 2,\\pm 4,\\pm 8\n$$\n\n- Let's pick $x=1.$ Substituting to the characteristic equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1)^{3}-6(1)^{2}-15(1)-8 & =-28.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $\\lambda =1$ is not a root of the equation.\n\n- Let's pick $x=-1.$ Substituting to the characteristic equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1)^{3}-6(-1)^{2}-15(-1)-8 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $\\lambda =-1$ is a root of the equation.\n\nSo, we can factor $(\\lambda +1)$ out of ${\\lambda }^{3}-6{\\lambda }^{2}-15\\lambda -8$ using synthetic division:\n\n| $-1$ | $1$ | $-6$ | $-15$ | $-8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $↓$ | $-1$ | $7$ | $8$ |\n|  | $1$ | $-7$ | $-8$ | $0$ |\n\nSo, we obtain the following factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda +1)({\\lambda }^{2}-7\\lambda -8) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -8) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-1,$ and $\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=8.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Eigenvalues of a General 3x3 Matrix"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124571 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124380 :question/id #uuid "a1c51187-c0a6-505c-bc58-2319b439086e" :question/math-academy-id "e-7047" :question/problem "![](images/2e/2e17e4fa743f6f8d3f5987b9095cf6976ae8eadf36ee4456ea8a9195201526e4.svg)\n\nConsider the matrix $P$ given above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\lambda=4$ is an eigenvalue of $P$\n\nII. $\\lambda=-1$ is an eigenvalue of $P$\n\nIII. The eigenvalue $\\lambda=6$ has algebraic multiplicity $2$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\, P-\\lambda I \\mathbin{:}$\n﻿﻿﻿![](images/38/38316eff018e61b4f9f6ce90e0e231ed1eeb6fe993f3b107a5ad8057e3641fd4.svg)\n\nThe characteristic equation is $\\det(P-\\lambda I) = 0.$ \n\nNotice that we can expand the $4 \\times 4$ determinant across the $1$st column, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 0 & -8 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1-\\lambda  & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 4-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 7 & -3 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, expanding the $3 \\times 3$ determinant across the $2$nd row, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3-\\lambda )\\cdot (4-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & 5 \\\\ 7 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )((-1-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )-35) & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-36) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -6)(\\lambda +6) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the eigenvalues of $P$ are $\\lambda=3,$ $\\lambda=4,$ $\\lambda=6,$ and $\\lambda=-6$ (all with algebraic multiplicity $1$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef311af0-0e95-5574-a151-2971ad66bd08" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125011 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "414f9370-14a3-5aa6-8486-cea2e27301a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -2)^{2}(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -5)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447397} {:answer/id #uuid "457e9051-86d9-52ea-9195-8e29a88ad83f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -2)(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -5)(\\lambda -1)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447398} {:answer/id #uuid "691f275b-fd9a-54d9-8586-a64a1a03045b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -2)(\\lambda -5)^{2}(\\lambda +1)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447409} {:answer/id #uuid "75cdd761-23be-5c11-826b-34cb06e74a70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -2)^{2}(\\lambda -5)^{2}=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447415} {:answer/id #uuid "8bcf654c-f10a-5880-a4ae-224b5c7e4e07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -2)(\\lambda -5)(\\lambda +1)^{2}=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447423}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -2)(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -5)(\\lambda -1)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447398} :answer-field/id #uuid "34c56093-04e6-5946-b523-0fde12c0770a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122666}] :question/id #uuid "d28aed4f-dd9b-57fa-bc7d-1ecf9008bea3" :question/math-academy-id "q-36819" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 5 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,B-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nB-\\lambda I=\\begin{bmatrix}2-\\lambda  & 5 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1-\\lambda  & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(B-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nSince the determinant of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix is given by the product of the entries on the main diagonal, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}2-\\lambda  & 5 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1-\\lambda  & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(-1-\\lambda )(5-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -2)(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -5)(\\lambda -1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125062 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "203333e3-42b8-50e5-ad7c-349f412c474d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448596} {:answer/id #uuid "909fc2e1-73fa-59b2-a46b-d44dc0bb0b16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448597}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448596} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a9cdab4-a97f-58e7-b97a-81f65eb22730" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449338} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6017700f-5a71-5853-a457-72bd0d6622d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448598} {:answer/id #uuid "78230748-a3fa-5d9d-9caf-d1ef1fc40fb5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448599}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448599} :answer-field/id #uuid "baf3d724-150e-5574-a988-4d93412ca0c2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449339} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f182a3b9-57f6-551f-b745-0c46637db13b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448600} {:answer/id #uuid "9f9693de-9b5c-55ce-8c6f-86871ae8c865" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448601}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448601} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5f31ab0-0b07-530a-931a-fd795892e749" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449340}] :question/id #uuid "c699a77c-6393-5572-b010-6743d9f3bb17" :question/math-academy-id "q-37355" :question/problem "$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -9 & -18 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -10 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -10 & 0 \\\\ -18 & 18 & -36 & -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $P$ given above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\lambda =-1$ is an eigenvalue of $P$\n\n- **II.** $\\lambda =-10$ is an eigenvalue of $P$\n\n- **III.** The eigenvalue $\\lambda =-10$ has algebraic multiplicity $3$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,P-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nP-\\lambda I=\\begin{bmatrix}-1-\\lambda  & -9 & -18 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -10-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -10-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -18 & 18 & -36 & -4-\\lambda \\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(P-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nNotice that we can expand the $4\\times 4$ determinant across the $2$nd row, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-1-\\lambda  & -9 & -18 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -10-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -10-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -18 & 18 & -36 & -4-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (-10-\\lambda )\\begin{vmatrix}-1-\\lambda  & -18 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -10-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -18 & -36 & -4-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, expanding the $3\\times 3$ determinant across the $2$nd row, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-10-\\lambda )\\cdot (-10-\\lambda )\\begin{vmatrix}-1-\\lambda  & -3 \\\\ -18 & -4-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (-10-\\lambda )^{2}((-1-\\lambda )(-4-\\lambda )-54) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +10)^{2}({\\lambda }^{2}+5\\lambda -50) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +10)^{2}(\\lambda +10)(\\lambda -5) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +10)^{3}(\\lambda -5) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the eigenvalues of $P$ are $\\lambda =-10$ (with algebraic multiplicity $3$) and $\\lambda =5.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272092 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb643844-0c56-5e23-9937-c4d548e084c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449562} {:answer/id #uuid "8a4b9bd6-2a00-59a9-a615-c97c3e869865" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449563}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449563} :answer-field/id #uuid "136321e8-01a0-5e29-b277-512685edf90f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450735} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97521b78-12e0-5c5d-8379-a7c0b43deff5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449564} {:answer/id #uuid "2e911fcf-5da4-5773-a35d-f09f35516166" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449565}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449565} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f2d1ae9-8c9e-5ac2-a9bb-09e86348c551" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450736} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fbac379-e615-5a86-9163-aad1e70a6e39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449566} {:answer/id #uuid "9cdbec38-3b6f-5e45-a26d-04e807074a86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449567}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449566} :answer-field/id #uuid "04180575-beb1-59bc-83ca-8f929f6a729f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450737}] :question/id #uuid "a042e23b-9a4b-5f08-a06a-17d78f4dd358" :question/math-academy-id "q-140450" :question/problem "$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 & -6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -4 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $P$ given above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\lambda =0$ is an eigenvalue of $P$\n- **II.** $\\lambda =-4$ is an eigenvalue of $P$\n- **III.** The eigenvalue $\\lambda =2$ has algebraic multiplicity $2$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,P-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nP-\\lambda I=\\begin{bmatrix}5-\\lambda  & 2 & -6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -\\lambda  & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -4-\\lambda  & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2-\\lambda \\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(P-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nNotice that we can expand the $4\\times 4$ determinant across the $1$st column, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}5-\\lambda  & 2 & -6 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -\\lambda  & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -4-\\lambda  & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (5-\\lambda )\\begin{vmatrix}-\\lambda  & 0 & 7 \\\\ -3 & -4-\\lambda  & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, expanding the $3\\times 3$ determinant across the $3$rd row, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(5-\\lambda )\\cdot (2-\\lambda )\\begin{vmatrix}-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -3 & -4-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (5-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda )(-\\lambda )(-4-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -5)(\\lambda -2)\\lambda (\\lambda +4) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the eigenvalues of $P$ are $\\lambda =5,$ $\\lambda =2,$ $\\lambda =0,$ and $\\lambda =-4$  (all with algebraic multiplicity $1$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272102 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44aa4cfa-3180-5442-8e75-ba1c05ae3cc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +4)(\\lambda -8)(\\lambda +5)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269895} {:answer/id #uuid "591dd63a-d199-5e93-bfbb-a40b87a92c10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -7)(\\lambda +4)(\\lambda +5)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270057} {:answer/id #uuid "6e9bd84c-c861-54af-897d-8ef317304806" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -7)(\\lambda +4)(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -5)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270251} {:answer/id #uuid "8e737deb-7b2b-5c10-a2f1-ff581e3be55f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -7)(\\lambda +4)(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +5)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270503} {:answer/id #uuid "fa8c69b0-ffdb-53b4-9343-e90d90da6e9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda +7)(\\lambda +4)(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -2)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271458}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -7)(\\lambda +4)(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +5)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270503} :answer-field/id #uuid "95b21e22-4684-5abe-87a1-7e9e493eb9bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271775}] :question/id #uuid "61624282-afa1-5aa5-87a3-f50541d7253a" :question/math-academy-id "q-140471" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$P=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 6 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,P-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nP-\\lambda I=\\begin{bmatrix}7-\\lambda  & 6 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4-\\lambda  & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3-\\lambda  & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -5-\\lambda \\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(P-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nSince the determinant of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix is given by the product of the entries on the main diagonal, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}7-\\lambda  & 6 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4-\\lambda  & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3-\\lambda  & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -5-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (7-\\lambda )(-4-\\lambda )(3-\\lambda )(-5-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -7)(\\lambda +4)(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +5) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323856 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37b6ac24-0c1e-5fc9-b42e-8ef4cc710cc6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -6)(\\lambda +6)(\\lambda +7)(\\lambda +2)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321572} {:answer/id #uuid "40deb6cc-8bb8-569c-97f3-3fcc4e19a6a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -6)(\\lambda +7)(\\lambda +2)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321663} {:answer/id #uuid "8b521092-f07a-5895-9682-3a649725784f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -6)^{2}(\\lambda +7)(\\lambda +2)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322258} {:answer/id #uuid "99c0a06e-b7ea-5030-8aaa-75f9242864b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -6)^{2}(\\lambda -7)(\\lambda -2)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322368} {:answer/id #uuid "c255b39b-f63a-5ec5-a34b-d0da65c605df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -6)(\\lambda +6)(\\lambda -7)(\\lambda -2)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322655}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -6)^{2}(\\lambda +7)(\\lambda +2)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322258} :answer-field/id #uuid "215ff11e-8e2f-5d56-9a14-7f0f6d5650dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323231}] :question/id #uuid "6825b6f2-ad84-5b7b-81c9-946e962a690f" :question/math-academy-id "q-36843" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=\\begin{bmatrix}6-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -7-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2-\\lambda \\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(A-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nSince the determinant of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix is given by the product of the entries on the main diagonal, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}6-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -7-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -2-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (6-\\lambda )(-7-\\lambda )(6-\\lambda )(-2-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -6)^{2}(\\lambda +7)(\\lambda +2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354507 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "242bc1ff-9d6a-5249-9c87-df81d32a7785" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -2)(\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +3)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351897} {:answer/id #uuid "4ca0ab54-3950-52f9-9f8a-4d77319ad175" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -3)^{2}(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda -1)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352267} {:answer/id #uuid "4fbc21b4-be4d-543a-b434-958a7eefccf3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +3)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352287} {:answer/id #uuid "c609ae85-57e2-57a3-9e3e-63455f2e5cd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -3)^{2}(\\lambda -2)(\\lambda -1)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353284} {:answer/id #uuid "ea8f1d9a-964d-5721-a11c-a90ebcc3202e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda +{3}^{2})(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda -1)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353612}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +3)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352287} :answer-field/id #uuid "709448bf-2e7d-5b59-85e2-71d9ceccca7a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354027}] :question/id #uuid "f5c38096-9f20-5f16-82a1-f8397b703a46" :question/math-academy-id "q-86749" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$P=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 5 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,P-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nP-\\lambda I=\\begin{bmatrix}3-\\lambda  & 5 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2-\\lambda  & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1-\\lambda  & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3-\\lambda \\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(P-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nSince the determinant of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix is given by the product of the entries on the main diagonal, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}3-\\lambda  & 5 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2-\\lambda  & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1-\\lambda  & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )(-2-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )(-3-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366006 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e7e5456c-c3dd-5a0d-b1c2-3704fc8684a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451347} {:answer/id #uuid "2e3a06ba-b64e-5195-8730-c9b460991557" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451348}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451347} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1d9b580-5d43-50e2-927e-f8ae49947f12" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452521} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44f80825-4dc0-5703-964c-52ef15f73d55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451349} {:answer/id #uuid "183ba4dd-4b07-51c8-addc-3f2d2bef0202" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451350}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451350} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e54440b-ec3a-55ca-8152-eddfc8c269f2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452522} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd8399ad-e6d4-5375-a818-f30592990e92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451351} {:answer/id #uuid "171f1a31-d670-547d-9146-cec5d20385e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451352}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451352} :answer-field/id #uuid "b104c177-2725-5efd-84ea-448298f66c5d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452523}] :question/id #uuid "e41ff16d-c666-5918-91e3-4e187ca2af95" :question/math-academy-id "q-37387" :question/problem "$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -7 & 6 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $C$ given above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\lambda =2$ is an eigenvalue of $C$\n\n- **II.** $\\lambda =5$ is an eigenvalue of $C$\n\n- **III.** The eigenvalue $\\lambda =5$ has algebraic multiplicity $2$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,C-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nC-\\lambda I=\\begin{bmatrix}2-\\lambda  & 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 2 & -3-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 1 & -7 & 6 & 5-\\lambda \\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(C-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nNotice that we can expand the $4\\times 4$ determinant across the $4$th column, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}2-\\lambda  & 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 2 & -3-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 1 & -7 & 6 & 5-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (5-\\lambda )\\begin{vmatrix}2-\\lambda  & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -5 & 2 & -3-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, expanding the $3\\times 3$ determinant across the $2$nd row, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(5-\\lambda )\\cdot (5-\\lambda )\\begin{vmatrix}2-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ -5 & -3-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (5-\\lambda )^{2}\\cdot ((2-\\lambda )(-3-\\lambda )+20) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -5)^{2}({\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda +14) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $D<0$ for the polynomial ${\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda +14$ we have that the only real eigenvalue is $\\lambda =5$ (with algebraic multiplicity $2$). \n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366365 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86ec9910-e0fd-500c-a549-944d8205800e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451789} {:answer/id #uuid "5a37d4f9-58db-5ba8-88b3-85410ad5ea6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451790}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451790} :answer-field/id #uuid "d02090ef-d4ce-52dc-a572-f7d577aef6d1" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452742} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5bd5e478-5cfa-5b4b-b744-a3677754f14d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451791} {:answer/id #uuid "0b89ae10-1176-5228-9818-87068f6baeb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451792}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451792} :answer-field/id #uuid "5f49c755-7208-571d-b62b-fa250286bf1d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452743} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d81aeff-94a5-5d39-a36b-e4ef94203480" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451793} {:answer/id #uuid "1923b6cb-681f-5678-aa63-c64a0628a021" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451794}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451793} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba776b6a-55ef-5233-8b4a-47f605e790d5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452744}] :question/id #uuid "c6753a04-a08e-5bc2-a11a-2cad03fb8d3f" :question/math-academy-id "q-80800" :question/problem "$$\nP=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & -8 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -2 & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -14\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $P$ given above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\lambda =0$ is an eigenvalue of $P$\n\n- **II.** $\\lambda =-14$ is an eigenvalue of $P$\n\n- **III.** The eigenvalue $\\lambda =2$ has algebraic multiplicity $2$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,P-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nP-\\lambda I=\\begin{bmatrix}2-\\lambda  & -3 & -8 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -\\lambda  & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -2-\\lambda  & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -14-\\lambda \\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(P-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nNotice that we can expand the $4\\times 4$ determinant across the $1$st column, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}2-\\lambda  & -3 & -8 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -\\lambda  & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -2-\\lambda  & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -14-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )\\begin{vmatrix}-\\lambda  & 0 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -2-\\lambda  & 11 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -14-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, expanding the $3\\times 3$ determinant across the $3$rd row, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2-\\lambda )\\cdot (-14-\\lambda )\\begin{vmatrix}-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(-14-\\lambda )(-\\lambda )(-2-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -2)(\\lambda +14)\\lambda (\\lambda +2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the eigenvalues of $P$ are $\\lambda =2,$ $\\lambda =-2,$ $\\lambda =0,$ and $\\lambda =-14$  (all with algebraic multiplicity $1$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366511 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d3139a9d-4709-52dc-b082-fa6e7262b4f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451863} {:answer/id #uuid "6611bee2-086e-5458-82d6-29162e06ef7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451864}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451864} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b3c705f-a12e-5ec7-9d9e-7cfb964eab33" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452779} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "80fd8012-3fa3-5669-b4d0-1a4677a6674d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451865} {:answer/id #uuid "f4d74f60-32b7-5c05-af9d-16a41f64d1c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451866}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451866} :answer-field/id #uuid "061f5f16-a1a6-5a40-b334-2790c7680235" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452780} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ceb7b4d4-53de-5934-8e1a-b0b8206b39b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451867} {:answer/id #uuid "3f9d8d40-8af7-502f-800e-af1a162fcfc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451868}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186451868} :answer-field/id #uuid "a5bb764e-2d9e-5196-a9d1-56181fe324ba" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452781}] :question/id #uuid "5ad99f7f-a225-5eb9-a085-4dc337f7e2b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-86752" :question/problem "$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $D$ given above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $\\lambda =2$ is an eigenvalue of $D$\n\n- **II.** $\\lambda =-1$ is an eigenvalue of $D$\n\n- **III.** The eigenvalue $\\lambda =-1$ has algebraic multiplicity $2$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,D-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nD-\\lambda I=\\begin{bmatrix}-1-\\lambda  & -2 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1-\\lambda  & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -\\lambda  & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -7-\\lambda \\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(D-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nNotice that we can expand the $4\\times 4$ determinant across the $1$st column, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(D-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-1-\\lambda  & -2 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1-\\lambda  & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -\\lambda  & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -7-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (-1-\\lambda )\\begin{vmatrix}1-\\lambda  & -1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -\\lambda  & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, expanding the $3\\times 3$ determinant across the $3$rd row, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1-\\lambda )(-7-\\lambda )\\begin{vmatrix}1-\\lambda  & -1 \\\\ -2 & -\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (-1-\\lambda )(-7-\\lambda )((1-\\lambda )(-\\lambda )-2) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)(\\lambda +7)({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -2) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)(\\lambda +7)(\\lambda -2)(\\lambda +1) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)^{2}(\\lambda +7)(\\lambda -2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the eigenvalues of $D$ are $\\lambda =-1$ (with algebraic multiplicity $2$), $\\lambda =-7$ and $\\lambda =2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442271 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0069a32c-24a8-592d-aebc-701756d8bdcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442259} {:answer/id #uuid "8e52e58b-8a75-5be5-b33c-025f9395fdc7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442264} {:answer/id #uuid "95f7c606-fabc-51e1-8528-9632cdd50f62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442265} {:answer/id #uuid "c80a4f86-8e3e-57b3-9a46-45e60e433bf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442267} {:answer/id #uuid "f29dc51e-2c92-5c6d-8ac3-24dd5e961743" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442268}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442265} :answer-field/id #uuid "24804dcb-504d-588f-82a7-fb6fe2bd5e63" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442269}] :question/id #uuid "970b7afa-4ca1-5d4a-a4eb-b7279227d558" :question/math-academy-id "q-37356" :question/problem "$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $B$ given above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\lambda =-5$ is an eigenvalue of $B$\n\nII. $\\lambda =-1$ is an eigenvalue of $B$\n\nIII. The eigenvalue $\\lambda =-3$ has algebraic multiplicity $2$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,B-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nB-\\lambda I=\\begin{bmatrix}-5-\\lambda  & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3-\\lambda  & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & -1-\\lambda \\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(B-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nNotice that we can expand the $4\\times 4$ determinant across the $1$st column, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}-5-\\lambda  & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3-\\lambda  & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 & -1-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (-5-\\lambda )\\begin{vmatrix}3-\\lambda  & 0 & -2 \\\\ 7 & -3-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ 5 & 0 & -1-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, expanding the $3\\times 3$ determinant across the $2$nd column, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-5-\\lambda )\\cdot (-3-\\lambda )\\begin{vmatrix}3-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 5 & -1-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (-5-\\lambda )\\cdot (-3-\\lambda )((3-\\lambda )(-1-\\lambda )+10) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +5)(\\lambda +3)({\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +7) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $D<0$ for the polynomial ${\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +7$, we have that the only real eigenvalues are $\\lambda =-5$ and $\\lambda =-3$ (both with algebraic multiplicity $1$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447465 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "040615ac-cb0a-5fce-99f6-4ed63d75aaeb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -5)(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda +4)(\\lambda -1)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447376} {:answer/id #uuid "2498f497-cc93-5d6b-a1c8-83b43853b063" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda +5)(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -1)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447388} {:answer/id #uuid "26c14220-eceb-59a1-9b09-b87b97b8a7b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -5)(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -1)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447389} {:answer/id #uuid "2cd374ea-5661-54f0-b4f0-721321849bb9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -5)(\\lambda -4)(\\lambda +1)^{2}=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447391} {:answer/id #uuid "f9560526-e72e-5f8b-ab9e-5ebe403d5441" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -5)(\\lambda +4)(\\lambda -1)^{2}=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447448}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -5)(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -1)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447389} :answer-field/id #uuid "834cc150-7558-5f94-8ad6-94ae5f3cfbc7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447457}] :question/id #uuid "243cda6a-277e-5555-a0d1-a4b1a66521e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-37353" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=\\begin{bmatrix}5-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -1-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 4-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -3 & 1-\\lambda \\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(A-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nSince the determinant of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix is given by the product of the entries on the main diagonal, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}5-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -1-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 4-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -3 & 1-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (5-\\lambda )(-1-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -5)(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447473 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09eda0ec-8e1b-5e11-a68f-03dfb4b379e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda -7)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447378} {:answer/id #uuid "7638f82e-310a-5356-96a6-5573794cce10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -2)(\\lambda +7)(\\lambda +2)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447416} {:answer/id #uuid "d612d7a1-320d-5230-8d43-429cf1f224b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda -7)(\\lambda -2)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447443} {:answer/id #uuid "e44519c4-103d-5ede-bc2f-bccaf86b7bee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -1)(\\lambda -2)^{2}(\\lambda -7)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447445} {:answer/id #uuid "f3ff7a34-01f9-5d59-a7ea-85ad5c394bee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +2)^{2}(\\lambda -7)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447447}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda -7)(\\lambda -2)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447443} :answer-field/id #uuid "506939ed-7e7a-58fe-a23e-568138385abc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447453}] :question/id #uuid "d00c6bd7-a884-5180-8cfd-0ffa34fc590f" :question/math-academy-id "q-86751" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$E=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 7 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,E-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nE-\\lambda I=\\begin{bmatrix}1-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -2-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 7-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 & 2-\\lambda \\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(E-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nSince the determinant of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix is given by the product of the entries on the main diagonal, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(E-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}1-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -2-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 7-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 & 2-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )(-2-\\lambda )(7-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda -7)(\\lambda -2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a 4x4 Matrix Containing a Block of Zeros"}] :topic/math-academy-id 1964 :topic/title "The Characteristic Equation of a Matrix"}] [{:activity/_scope [{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101678} :activity/id #uuid "d19bc789-6fc7-5102-bc7b-8f270f9b39a8" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101678 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101959 :tutorial/content "When multiplying two matrices in general, we apply the same approach as usual:\n\n- First, we verify that the two matrices are conformable for multiplication.\n\n- Then, we multiply each row in the first matrix by each column in the second.\n\nFor example, let's find $AB,$ where \n$\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\n\nFirst, we verify the conformability for multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\times \\color{green}{\\fbox{3}}}{A} \\underset{\\color{green}\\checkmark}{\\cdot} \\underset{{\\color{green}\\fbox{3}} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{B} = \n\t\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{C}\n$$\n\nSo the matrices are conformable for multiplication, and the product is a $2 \\times 2$ matrix. Let's set up the multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign {\n\t\\underbrace{\n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\begin{matrix}\n        -2 & 2 & 1  \\\\\n\t1 & -1 & 3 \n    \\end{matrix}\n    \\right\\rbrack}_{A}\n\n\t\\underbrace{\n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\begin{matrix}\n        -5 & 2   \\\\\n\t2 & -2   \\\\\n\t-4 & 1 \n    \\end{matrix}\n    \\right\\rbrack}_{B}\n\n\t&= \n\t\\underbrace{\n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\begin{matrix}\n        \\ast & \\ast   \\\\\n        \\ast & \\ast \n    \\end{matrix}\n    \\right\\rbrack\n\t}_{C}\n}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the entries of the product matrix (shown as $\\ast$'s in the equation above).\n\nTo find $c_{11},$ the entry at the intersection of the $1$st row and $1$st column, we calculate the dot product of the $1$st row of $A$ and the $1$st column of $B\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign {\n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\begin{matrix}\n        \\color{blue}-2 & \\color{blue}2 & \\color{blue}1  \\\\\n\t\\color{lightgray}1 & \\color{lightgray}-1 & \\color{lightgray}3 \n    \\end{matrix}\n    \\right\\rbrack\n\n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\begin{matrix}\n         \\color{red}-5 & \\color{lightgray}2   \\\\\n\t\\color{red}2 & \\color{lightgray}-2   \\\\\n\t\\color{red}-4 & \\color{lightgray}1\n    \\end{matrix}\n    \\right\\rbrack\n\n%\t&= \n%    \\left\\lbrack\n%   \\begin{matrix}\n%       ({\\color{blue}{-2}}) \\cdot ({\\color{red}{-5}}) + {\\color{blue}{2}} \\cdot {\\color{red}{2}} + {\\color{blue}{1}} \\cdot ({\\color{red}{-4}}) & \\ast   \\\\\n%        \\ast & \\ast\n%    \\end{matrix}\n%    \\right\\rbrack\n\n\t= \\left\\lbrack\n    \\begin{matrix}\n        \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{10} & \\ast   \\\\\n        \\ast & \\ast\n    \\end{matrix}\n    \\right\\rbrack, && \\quad \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{10} = ({\\color{blue}{-2}}) \\cdot ({\\color{red}{-5}}) + {\\color{blue}{2}} \\cdot {\\color{red}{2}} + {\\color{blue}{1}} \\cdot ({\\color{red}{-4}})\n}\n$$\n\nTo find $c_{12},$ we calculate the dot product of the $1$st row of $A$ and the $2$nd column of $B\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign {\n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\begin{matrix}\n        \\color{blue}-2 & \\color{blue}2 & \\color{blue}1  \\\\\n\t\\color{lightgray}1 & \\color{lightgray}-1 & \\color{lightgray}3 \n    \\end{matrix}\n    \\right\\rbrack\n\n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\begin{matrix}\n        \\color{lightgray}-5 & \\color{red}2   \\\\\n\t\\color{lightgray}2 & \\color{red}-2   \\\\\n\t\\color{lightgray}-4 & \\color{red}1\n    \\end{matrix}\n    \\right\\rbrack\n\n%\t&= \n%    \\left\\lbrack\n%    \\begin{matrix}\n%        10 & ({\\color{blue}{-2}}) \\cdot {\\color{red}{2}} + {\\color{blue}{2}} \\cdot ({\\color{red}{-2}}) + {\\color{blue}{1}} \\cdot {\\color{red}{1}}   \\\\\n%        \\ast & \\ast\n%    \\end{matrix}\n%    \\right\\rbrack\n\n\t= \\left\\lbrack\n    \\begin{matrix}\n        10 & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{-7}   \\\\\n        \\ast & \\ast\n    \\end{matrix}\n    \\right\\rbrack, && \\quad \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{-7} = ({\\color{blue}{-2}}) \\cdot {\\color{red}{2}} + {\\color{blue}{2}} \\cdot ({\\color{red}{-2}}) + {\\color{blue}{1}} \\cdot {\\color{red}{1}}\n}\n$$\n\nTo find $c_{21},$ we calculate the dot product of the $2$nd row of $A$ and the $1$st column of $B\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign {\n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\begin{matrix}\n        \\color{lightgray}-2 & \\color{lightgray}2 & \\color{lightgray}1  \\\\\n\t\\color{blue}1 & \\color{blue}-1 & \\color{blue}3 \n    \\end{matrix}\n    \\right\\rbrack\n\n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\begin{matrix}\n         \\color{red}-5 & \\color{lightgray}2   \\\\\n\t\\color{red}2 & \\color{lightgray}-2   \\\\\n\t\\color{red}-4 & \\color{lightgray}1\n    \\end{matrix}\n    \\right\\rbrack\n\n%\t&= \n%    \\left\\lbrack\n%    \\begin{matrix}\n%        10 & -7   \\\\\n%        {\\color{blue}{1}} \\cdot ({\\color{red}{-5}}) + ({\\color{blue}{-1}}) \\cdot {\\color{red}{2}} + {\\color{blue}{3}} \\cdot ({\\color{red}{-4}}) & \\ast\n%    \\end{matrix}\n%    \\right\\rbrack\n\n\t= \\left\\lbrack\n    \\begin{matrix}\n        10 & -7   \\\\\n        \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{-19} & \\ast\n    \\end{matrix}\n    \\right\\rbrack, && \\quad \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{-19} = {\\color{blue}{1}} \\cdot ({\\color{red}{-5}}) + ({\\color{blue}{-1}}) \\cdot {\\color{red}{2}} + {\\color{blue}{3}} \\cdot ({\\color{red}{-4}})\n}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find $c_{22},$ we calculate the dot product of the $2$nd row of $A$ and the $2$nd column of $B\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\eqalign {\n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\begin{matrix}\n        \\color{lightgray}-2 & \\color{lightgray}2 & \\color{lightgray}1  \\\\\n\t\\color{blue}1 & \\color{blue}-1 & \\color{blue}3 \n    \\end{matrix}\n    \\right\\rbrack\n\n    \\left\\lbrack\n    \\begin{matrix}\n        \\color{lightgray}-5 & \\color{red}2   \\\\\n\t\\color{lightgray}2 & \\color{red}-2   \\\\\n\t\\color{lightgray}-4 & \\color{red}1\n    \\end{matrix}\n    \\right\\rbrack\n\n%\t&= \n%    \\left\\lbrack\n%    \\begin{matrix}\n%        10 & -7   \\\\\n%        -19 & {\\color{blue}{1}} \\cdot {\\color{red}{2}} + ({\\color{blue}{-1}}) \\cdot ({\\color{red}{-2}}) + {\\color{blue}{3}} \\cdot {\\color{red}{1}}\n%    \\end{matrix}\n%    \\right\\rbrack\n\n\t= \\left\\lbrack\n    \\begin{matrix}\n        10 & -7   \\\\\n        -19 & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{7}\n    \\end{matrix}\n    \\right\\rbrack, && \\quad \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{7} = {\\color{blue}{1}} \\cdot {\\color{red}{2}} + ({\\color{blue}{-1}}) \\cdot ({\\color{red}{-2}}) + {\\color{blue}{3}} \\cdot {\\color{red}{1}}\n}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n$\\begin{bmatrix}10 & -7 \\\\ -19 & 7\\end{bmatrix}$" :tutorial/id #uuid "ce402944-0109-5d9d-93d5-394323fbc469" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2993 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "190a2922-1a7b-53bc-995b-5efd5caf84b2" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101679}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101679 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100872 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92dd864a-8bc0-547c-84c9-ffd562909315"} :step/id #uuid "864b056d-3d24-5ade-a901-89324e218c5c" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101681}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101680 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101960 :tutorial/content "It's possible to express matrix multiplication using index notation.\n\nTo see how, first let $C=AB,$ where $A$ and $B$ are two matrices that are conformable for multiplication.\n\nThen $c_{\\color{red}{i}\\color{blue}{j}}$ represents the entry at the intersection of the $\\color{red}i$th row and $\\color{blue}j$th column in $C.$\n\nTo compute $c_{\\color{red}{i}\\color{blue}{j}},$ we take the dot product of the $\\color{red}i$th row of $\\color{red}A$ and the $\\color{blue}j$th column of ${\\color{blue}B},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{i1} & {a}_{i2} & ⋯ & {a}_{in}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "4b8d43b0-7ded-5276-9ed1-766d5f5fff93" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2994 :tutorial/title "Index Notation of Matrix Multiplication"} :step/id #uuid "bc9f1c5d-87d6-5b08-95da-74e0d5064eae"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101681 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100873 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "71ff07eb-2e16-529e-b17c-1bf7cb9703bd"} :step/id #uuid "09c42d8b-5f21-5e0f-b672-291ed8dc0ef2" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101746}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101746 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100913 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d7d67c6-d54f-5ee1-af59-fd63d6687cfd"} :step/id #uuid "5035fe4b-368c-58ab-b199-a822b124d694" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101680}}] :activity/title "Multiplying Matrices" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186101055}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186050407 :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100872 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100694 :question/id #uuid "66ec04a0-2af8-5187-98b2-b06eedd5b0a8" :question/math-academy-id "e-4406" :question/problem "Find $CD$, if \n![](images/1a/1a753977affc5cc3dda18c9206116e1132254bccebd1e3f2545bea75bcc38f18.png)\nand \n![](images/b9/b99016bca94adc5de11eddef950fa13fc4349aaf95387468d07f294c409d029d.png)" :question/worked-solution "Here, $C$ is a $2 \\times 3$ matrix and $D$ is a $3 \\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $C$ and $3$ rows in $D,$ so $C$ and $D$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\times \\color{green}{\\fbox{3}}}{C} \\underset{\\color{green}\\checkmark}{\\cdot} \\underset{{\\color{green}\\fbox{3}} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{D} = \n\t\\underset{\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} \\times \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2}}{CD}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $CD,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-4=1\\cdot 0+(-2)\\cdot 2+0\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 1 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,1=1\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot 0+0\\cdot 2 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-1=2\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 2+1\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,4=2\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ![](images/64/64b831a66cdd9a3176d1eb916dfae189b41eb1f0f3ed3184797f92e404957878.png)"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92dd864a-8bc0-547c-84c9-ffd562909315" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101102 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "802f0864-9cf0-558a-a018-182bdf8634b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 14 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186097948} {:answer/id #uuid "b691c70f-2540-52ab-8dcd-df9ba3df2032" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}14 & 14 \\\\ 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186097949} {:answer/id #uuid "fe65f2af-0005-5919-8f19-ecf1b9c126a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 14 \\\\ 14 & -4 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186097950} {:answer/id #uuid "1c72920d-772a-500b-9395-f0209f18233d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}14 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 14 & 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186097951} {:answer/id #uuid "26c0b3f2-4e44-50f1-8d01-c38b4bd3a2b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 14 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186097952}] :answer-field/id #uuid "f29037cd-0b30-58bb-838f-c0248d7bb442" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186097947}] :question/id #uuid "21a80dc1-b25f-5f4c-ad00-3158fc32fd15" :question/math-academy-id "q-1029" :question/problem "If\n$X = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$Y = \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$\nthen $XY =$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101104 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9930448b-7559-5035-9318-225253a10b76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}12 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186097960} {:answer/id #uuid "4ae7e1b7-47d1-5517-b3ce-af5022453d88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 54 \\\\ -3 & 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186097961} {:answer/id #uuid "5f8bab3b-f969-570c-9bba-8b1cbb9bc410" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}48 & 54 \\\\ 3 & -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186097962} {:answer/id #uuid "794420f1-b2c5-535e-8d7b-3bc881e4a12d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}48 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186097963} {:answer/id #uuid "7d26aa62-97bf-576f-8cad-734f8bb38e4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}48 & 3 \\\\ 54 & -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186097964}] :answer-field/id #uuid "6106ff27-a10c-5110-b526-56f147f3d77b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186097959}] :question/id #uuid "1af60e7f-3da3-56ec-8846-70fae5eeab59" :question/math-academy-id "q-1034" :question/problem "Find $AB$, if\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$B = \\begin{bmatrix}6 & 5 \\\\ 9 & 8 \\\\ 3 & 7\\end{bmatrix}$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237990 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0172af46-e351-502b-aa3a-c62166a7ed72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}18 & -2 \\\\ -15 & 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235806} {:answer/id #uuid "12333d71-f54d-5f6e-9e6c-5fc764d2bc80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 9 \\\\ -15 & 18\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235924} {:answer/id #uuid "442b8d6f-cd03-5b5a-84f1-23d1ca97ea2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}18 & -2 \\\\ 9 & 15\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236256} {:answer/id #uuid "7b37a294-1d3c-567d-bf66-b3920a5fe9a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}18 & -2 \\\\ 15 & 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236585} {:answer/id #uuid "8ce9cddf-2413-5e15-89c7-45b259cab3b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 18 \\\\ 15 & 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236707}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 18 \\\\ 15 & 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236707} :answer-field/id #uuid "a44f4bb4-30a2-5a30-959a-18587874cdc3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237655}] :question/id #uuid "53274149-3160-5be4-b6eb-415d49f449f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-1033" :question/problem "If\n$E=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$F=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$\nthen $EF=$" :question/worked-solution "Here, $E$ is a $2\\times 4$ matrix and $F$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $4$ columns in $E$ and $4$ rows in $F,$ so $E$ and $F$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{E}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{F}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 2}={EF}_{2\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $EF,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,2=1\\cdot 4+(-2)\\cdot (-3)+4\\cdot (-2)+5\\cdot 0 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 18 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,18=1\\cdot 2+(-2)\\cdot (-1)+4\\cdot 1+5\\cdot 2 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 18 \\\\ 15 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,15=3\\cdot 4+(-1)\\cdot (-3)+0\\cdot (-2)+1\\cdot 0 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ -3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 18 \\\\ 15 & 9\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,9=3\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot (-1)+0\\cdot 1+1\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$EF=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 18 \\\\ 15 & 9\\end{bmatrix}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186238011 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f7a62ec-13b8-543d-9616-121868053523" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}20 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236016} {:answer/id #uuid "22e57d49-7fd7-563f-abb5-64190ff4aa02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}20 & 24 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236039} {:answer/id #uuid "24e7f5a9-a414-5f74-91fa-736878205105" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}12 & -24\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236055} {:answer/id #uuid "6b9d6d90-f170-5014-9e02-b7a17b19bb73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-20 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186236497} {:answer/id #uuid "bf7d5586-3d96-5a03-86a4-ba2ed71c39b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}24 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237034}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}24 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237034} :answer-field/id #uuid "c96651e8-d8ed-5375-92a8-7fde59b35ca0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237698}] :question/id #uuid "83b01661-23af-5f73-bcb3-22f2f416f38b" :question/math-academy-id "q-1035" :question/problem "Find $ST$,  if  $S=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$ and $T=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, $S$ is a $1\\times 4$ matrix and $T$ is a $4\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $4$ columns in $S$ and $4$ rows in $T,$ so $S$ and $T$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{S}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{T}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 2}={ST}_{1\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $ST,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}24 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,24=2\\cdot 1+(-3)\\cdot 0+1\\cdot (-2)+4\\cdot 6 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 6 & 4\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}24 & 1\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,1=2\\cdot (-2)+(-3)\\cdot 4+1\\cdot 1+4\\cdot 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$ST=\\begin{bmatrix}24 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265743 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24d545a5-b2e6-5053-b8b6-37194c5c9aa5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 6 \\\\ -3 & 10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263315} {:answer/id #uuid "338b8f0e-6e8c-5003-a20f-65d3696dd73a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-15 & 3 \\\\ -9 & 10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263448} {:answer/id #uuid "40cea55b-6167-57c5-a2d6-7f87677038d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & 10 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263572} {:answer/id #uuid "53864c34-56a3-5553-afb8-033b263dcdea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 10 \\\\ -6 & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263719} {:answer/id #uuid "d6bc1bd7-12d4-51d7-8d46-edc046b147b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-15 & 10 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264868}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-15 & 3 \\\\ -9 & 10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263448} :answer-field/id #uuid "7f084fe2-5f6e-5af3-b0dc-03f636f5e40e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265467}] :question/id #uuid "78f7d23e-60ed-507c-b4f6-6101bce65778" :question/math-academy-id "q-129495" :question/problem "Find $AB$, if\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$\nand \n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "Here, $A$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix and $B$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere are $3$ columns in $A$ and $3$ rows in $B,$ so $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{A}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{3}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{3}}\\times 2}={AB}_{2\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $AB,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-15 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-15=2\\cdot (-3)+(-1)\\cdot 6+1\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-15 & 3 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,3=2\\cdot 2+(-1)\\cdot 5+1\\cdot 4 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-15 & 3 \\\\ -9 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-9=1\\cdot (-3)+0\\cdot 6+2\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-15 & 3 \\\\ -9 & 10\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,10=1\\cdot 2+0\\cdot 5+2\\cdot 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$AB=\\begin{bmatrix}-15 & 3 \\\\ -9 & 10\\end{bmatrix}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265744 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30980b36-8778-5a51-89b8-a81fc027883f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}22 & 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263413} {:answer/id #uuid "3bd13396-77b3-54fa-8ae9-6c7200fc84bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 12\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263533} {:answer/id #uuid "7e0eeffe-95e5-570e-9c36-aea6b4fd89db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}15 & 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264086} {:answer/id #uuid "975b44bb-df10-5292-a437-e855bf7bd551" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264299} {:answer/id #uuid "aee8c241-2555-5612-b6c3-afa60e199249"