io} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186237680}] :question/id #uuid "dc228162-bbed-5edc-ac18-77311da73b13" :question/math-academy-id "q-1038" :question/problem "$\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & -1\\end{bmatrix}=$" :question/worked-solution "Here, the first factor is $4\\times 1$ matrix and the second factor is a $1\\times 3$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in the first matrix and $1$ row in the second matrix, so the product is well defined:\n\n$$\n4\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}✓\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 3=4\\times 3\n$$\n\nComputing the product, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{bmatrix}-10 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & -1\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-10\\cdot 1 & -10\\cdot (-5) & -10\\cdot (-1) \\\\ 6\\cdot 1 & 6\\cdot (-5) & 6\\cdot (-1) \\\\ 0\\cdot 1 & 0\\cdot (-5) & 0\\cdot (-1) \\\\ 8\\cdot 1 & 8\\cdot (-5) & 8\\cdot (-1)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-10 & 50 & 10 \\\\ 6 & -30 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 8 & -40 & -8\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265792 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e376d53d-27f0-5be2-b35f-f4d91876ada1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264977} {:answer/id #uuid "eb678b62-e5ac-5a34-a142-98bf42189475" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ -9 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265054} {:answer/id #uuid "f85d4f26-7a1c-53cb-bb4f-7d6a715d2393" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -9 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265174} {:answer/id #uuid "fbcf0048-3a05-5c6a-a8a8-728a7671810b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265204} {:answer/id #uuid "fd313f4f-a74a-5051-a216-9b54910390f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265223}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ -9 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265054} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ad6ed81-a246-516c-a457-e881158c431f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265493}] :question/id #uuid "c109d94f-badb-560f-816a-dc72e0193e2a" :question/math-academy-id "q-129961" :question/problem "If\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$\nthen $AB=$" :question/worked-solution "Here, $A$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix and $B$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. \n\nThere is $1$ column in $A$ and $1$ row in $B,$ so $A$ and $B$ are conformable for multiplication: \n\n$$\n{A}_{2\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\cdot }_{✓}{B}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}={AB}_{2\\times 2}\n$$\n\nLet's compute $AB,$ one element at a time:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-3=-1\\cdot 3 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,1=(-1)\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ -9 & ∗\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,-9=(-3)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & \\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ -9 & 3\\end{bmatrix}, &  & \\,3=(-3)\\cdot (-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n$AB=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ -9 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265838 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1731f4d0-2e00-51db-8ba8-df32c1c91bc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 16 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 1 