ath} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365537}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365537} :answer-field/id #uuid "29e201c0-3a1a-538d-9101-9fec659b4d05" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365536}] :question/id #uuid "55b781aa-d29f-5fcc-876e-4fb67d5ab82b" :question/math-academy-id "q-279486" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.$ If $f(X)={X}^{2}+X-4$, find $f(B).$\n\n| $f(B)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & ={X}^{2}+X-4 \\\\  & ={X}^{2}+X-4I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(B)={B}^{2}+B-4I.$\n\nLet's calculate ${B}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{B}^{2} & =B\\cdot B \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 6 \\\\ -3 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(B):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(B) & ={B}^{2}+B-4I \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 6 \\\\ -3 & 7\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}-4\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 6 \\\\ -3 & 7\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2+0-4 & 6+2-0 \\\\ -3+(-1)-0 & 7+3-4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 8 \\\\ -4 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365538 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b2de13f-7428-5cf4-a15d-bb759547b2ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365540}] :an