=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$f(E)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-1}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-2}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">\n{{field-3}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"30px\">\n{{field-4}}\n</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & ={X}^{2}+4X-5 \\\\  & ={X}^{2}+4X-5I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(E)={E}^{2}+4E-5I.$\n\nLet's calculate ${E}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{E}^{2} & =E\\cdot E \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(E):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(E) & ={E}^{2}+4E-5I \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}+4\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}-5\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 4\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4+8-5 & 0+0-0 \\\\ 3+4-0 & 1+4-5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366302 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22d7958c-94ba-5de3-9243-e30601f76543" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366304} {:answer/id #uuid "b10801ca-f13a-57ad-8038-3828133145ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366305} {:answer/id #uuid "e55ee6b6-6cbe-5ecc-a66b-628ac43bc811" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366306} {:answer/id #uuid "1a296f4e-0f9b-50c7-9b4e-bd01d0b60375" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366307} {:answer/id #uuid "eba229a2-1a77-552c-9266-524a1d9a221b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366308}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366308} :answer-field/id #uuid "de3f2328-fa8d-5da1-9c29-ab9566101429" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366303}] :question/id #uuid "2869021c-9120-59a9-9952-6f0d251d0602" :question/math-academy-id "q-78347" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.$  Find $f(B)$ if $f(X)={X}^{2}+X+3.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & ={X}^{2}+X+3 \\\\  & ={X}^{2}+X+3I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(B)={B}^{2}+B+3I.$\n\nLet's calculate ${B}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{B}^{2} & =B\\cdot B \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(B):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(B) & ={B}^{2}+B+3I \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}+3\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0+2+3 & 0+1+0 \\\\ 0+(-4)+0 & 0+(-2)+3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366309 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "afe8d6d8-0a6d-5efd-a9c0-c468f00d3f21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 5 \\\\ -15 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366311} {:answer/id #uuid "d25a56e7-16c2-5f88-992b-3343761aa97c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}29 & 5 \\\\ -5 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366312} {:answer/id #uuid "e3f3e7d5-a5eb-5b88-94d1-ab28c0dfcffd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}29 & 5 \\\\ -15 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366313} {:answer/id #uuid "8d63f40b-f2ea-5001-ae5e-ff191217dc44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}29 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366314} {:answer/id #uuid "eb627ab1-f604-5f7b-aa59-eecf1c4e4f64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 9 \\\\ -15 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366315}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}29 & 5 \\\\ -15 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366313} :answer-field/id #uuid "176f723a-0a36-5ca0-a32a-8d6d6c5acf73" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366310}] :question/id #uuid "2a14c0ed-8414-58e1-8b26-a5335ab66e8a" :question/math-academy-id "q-78584" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $H=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$  Find $f(H)$ if $f(X)={X}^{2}+X+2.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & ={X}^{2}+X+2 \\\\  & ={X}^{2}+X+2I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(H)={H}^{2}+H+2I.$\n\nLet's calculate ${H}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{H}^{2} & =H\\cdot H \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}22 & 4 \\\\ -12 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(H):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(H) & ={H}^{2}+H+2I \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}22 & 4 \\\\ -12 & -2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}+2\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}22 & 4 \\\\ -12 & -2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}22+5+2 & 4+1+0 \\\\ -12-3+0 & -2-1+2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}29 & 5 \\\\ -15 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388132 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "67b616c2-ce6e-5c95-8648-dd89dbfaa3f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388134} {:answer/id #uuid "ca63b17e-8661-5864-bf17-dbc1f35dc340" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 6 \\\\ 9 & 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388135} {:answer/id #uuid "5cae900f-3b80-52ed-97df-eae2af51f956" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -6 \\\\ 9 & -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388136} {:answer/id #uuid "8a887fa4-9ae0-5c2c-ac17-c0d680bda859" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -3 \\\\ 9 & 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388137} {:answer/id #uuid "de5ea921-ae36-5369-bf56-d02193f5bc68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 6 \\\\ -6 & 9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388138}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 6 \\\\ 9 & 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388135} :answer-field/id #uuid "889964a6-0e86-53e7-a015-8ff79199c498" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388133}] :question/id #uuid "01490c7d-4c84-5d6b-914b-a1fab67bc26a" :question/math-academy-id "q-130681" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.$  Find $f(A)$ if $f(X)={X}^{2}-2X-8.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & ={X}^{2}-2X-8 \\\\  & ={X}^{2}-2X-8I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(A)={A}^{2}-2A-8I.$\n\nLet's calculate ${A}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2} & =A\\cdot A \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 10 \\\\ 15 & 22\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(A):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(A) & ={A}^{2}-2A-8I \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 10 \\\\ 15 & 22\\end{bmatrix}-2\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}-8\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 10 \\\\ 15 & 22\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -4 \\\\ -6 & -8\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7-2-8 & 10-4+0 \\\\ 15-6+0 & 22-8-8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 6 \\\\ 9 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388139 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c29b720-4600-5452-856a-0de6c5b2cbbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388141} {:answer/id #uuid "d78e56c2-19a5-58bf-aac5-d59f602172e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388142} {:answer/id #uuid "b2514912-db4d-511d-a89d-093ae0777083" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388143} {:answer/id #uuid "d3f1a29c-c2ff-5901-b277-ceaff0eb220f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388144} {:answer/id #uuid "adc7ac7b-e40f-5c06-9fee-5b824b5729d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388145}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388145} :answer-field/id #uuid "5decefa1-878b-5a33-98d2-b1ec4d4f6078" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388140}] :question/id #uuid "6097bb1d-9d7a-56b4-9d4d-09d460a9e165" :question/math-academy-id "q-130687" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $C=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find $f(C)$ if $f(X)={X}^{2}-X+5.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & ={X}^{2}-X+5 \\\\  & ={X}^{2}-X+5I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(C)={C}^{2}-C+5I.$\n\nLet's calculate ${C}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}^{2} & =C\\cdot C \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(C):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(C) & ={C}^{2}-C+5I \\\\  & =C-C+5I \\\\  & =5I \\\\  & =5\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186388146 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98d46de3-1964-521e-987f-3f87e63d14f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388148} {:answer/id #uuid "290eb367-b69e-51e9-b010-dd7d2e86e6ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388149} {:answer/id #uuid "8ec94462-c5a9-5b19-af43-e4fb15a1b17d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 4 \\\\ 12 & 7\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388150} {:answer/id #uuid "def69761-fa9a-5675-91a9-81ca5a36b65a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388151} {:answer/id #uuid "cdeec92a-fd20-575e-a12b-6d715aa8a4a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 4 \\\\ 12 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388152}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388149} :answer-field/id #uuid "56b6390d-ed7e-571e-81e8-62f931b08ef6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186388147}] :question/id #uuid "22954632-a7ef-5551-8cda-37dd0def8e71" :question/math-academy-id "q-130688" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $K=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.$ Find $f(K)$ if $f(X)={X}^{2}-4X+1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & ={X}^{2}-4X+1 \\\\  & ={X}^{2}-4X+I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(K)={K}^{2}-4K+I.$\n\nLet's calculate ${K}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{K}^{2} & =K\\cdot K \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 4 \\\\ 12 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(K):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(K) & ={K}^{2}-4K+I \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 4 \\\\ 12 & 7\\end{bmatrix}-4\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 4 \\\\ 12 & 7\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 4 \\\\ 12 & 8\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7-8+1 & 4-4-0 \\\\ 12-12+0 & 7-8+1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486363 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22af9faf-479c-5211-b924-d2a2ed0ab1ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 8\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485823} {:answer/id #uuid "4a573fe0-ecf3-566c-990e-bc2091d59ff5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 6 \\\\ 8 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485900} {:answer/id #uuid "c787cd72-628c-5183-a122-bb1328cc72f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 8\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486126} {:answer/id #uuid "dd037009-e252-5c9b-a802-118a15252803" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 8\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486169} {:answer/id #uuid "f294d9c4-87c6-5c05-8909-273b2ed447a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 8 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486206}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 8\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486126} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c461903-1b4b-5b26-ad15-a19492090b76" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486248}] :question/id #uuid "2224e8b1-e5b3-5120-9cd4-8c63afa14c71" :question/math-academy-id "q-78583" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $D=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$  Find $f(D)$ if $f(X)={X}^{2}-3X+5.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & ={X}^{2}-3X+5 \\\\  & ={X}^{2}-3X+5I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(D)={D}^{2}-3D+5I.$\n\nLet's calculate ${D}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}^{2} & =D\\cdot D \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(D):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(D) & ={D}^{2}-3D+5I \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}-3\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}+5\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 9 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4-3+5 & -3+9+0 \\\\ -1+3+0 & 3+0+5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486453 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25168437-2aa4-5977-952c-2051730ceff6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 \\\\ -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485826} {:answer/id #uuid "5b213e2b-cc6d-508a-a15f-3bf22cc91d0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485924} {:answer/id #uuid "8b991cf9-c833-51b6-a70c-6462ead85a65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486013} {:answer/id #uuid "caf9fadd-4204-560a-bbdd-f5a3d57450f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}10 & 1 \\\\ 20 & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486132} {:answer/id #uuid "e0dd670b-075f-5794-a254-3720ba484dbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}11 & 1 \\\\ 20 & 5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486176}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485924} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab274d63-ed23-5349-8036-9b61afae1797" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486307}] :question/id #uuid "ebea1a9b-d1dc-56a2-8933-0092e4727688" :question/math-academy-id "q-130673" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.$  Find $f(A)$ if $f(X)={X}^{2}+X-1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & ={X}^{2}+X-1 \\\\  & ={X}^{2}+X-I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(A)={A}^{2}+A-I.$\n\nLet's calculate ${A}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2} & =A\\cdot A \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(A):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(A) & ={A}^{2}+A-I \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1+3-1 & 0-2+0 \\\\ 0+4+0 & 1-3-1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Matrix Polynomial"}] :topic/math-academy-id 1725 :topic/title "Powers of Matrices"}] [{:activity/_scope [{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167805} :activity/id #uuid "dc2433b7-ae23-5d90-bbbf-4a05485b89d1" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167805 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186168154 :tutorial/content "Suppose we want to find the *maximum* value of the quadratic form \n\n$$\nQ(\\mathbf{x})=2x_1^2 + 4x_2^2,\n$$\n\n \n\nsubject to the constraint $\\| \\mathbf{x} \\| = 1.$ This type of problem is known as a **constrained optimization problem**.   \n\nSince our quadratic form $Q(\\mathbf{x})$ has no mixed term $x_1x_2$, we can find its maximum value for $\\| \\mathbf{x} || = 1$ using algebraic manipulation, as follows.\n\nFirst, notice that $x_1^2 \\geq 0.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n2x_1^2 \\leq 4x_1^2.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & \\le 4{x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =4({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $\\| \\mathbf{x} \\| = 1$ is equivalent to $x_1^2 + x_2^2 =1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2})=4(1)=4,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that \n\n$$\nQ(\\mathbf{x}) \\leq 4.\n$$\n\nSo, the value of $Q(\\mathbf{x})$ can be no greater than $4.$ But before we conclude that $4$ is the maximum, we need to make sure that $Q(\\mathbf{x})$ can actually attain the value $4.$ Can we find a vector $\\mathbf x,$ with  $\\| \\mathbf{x} || = 1,$ such that $Q(\\mathbf{x}) = 4?$\n\nIndeed, we can. Setting ![](images/af/afe399f75b9a73a1834b4d359e29ad4814bd99f81b1cf20ccaa211078dd19645.svg) we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2(0)^{2}+4(1)^{2} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $\\| \\mathbf{x} \\| = 1,$  the maximum value of $Q(\\mathbf{x})$ equals $4.$\n\nProceeding similarly, we can show that the minimum of $Q(\\mathbf{x})$ is equal to $2.$ \n\nGraphically, the situation can be visualized if we intersect the surface $z= {\\color{black}2x_1^2+4x_2^2}$ and the cylinder $\\color{black}x_1^2+x_2^2=1,$ as shown below:  \n\n![](images/39/39bfc05c9dd0733c1f4f867d21d1a5f018aacbf0ed91036a6f0981d701ba69d8.png)" :tutorial/id #uuid "bf2f75a6-c5dc-5dc6-bcc2-1c89fec829de" :tutorial/math-academy-id 7952 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "b1874b80-07fb-5d4d-9fd9-46c46098d2a0" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167806}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167806 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166890 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a8666dd9-b763-589d-8ae3-af203068f1a4"} :step/id #uuid "396a0949-2648-520d-b31c-049c70bbd0c2" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167807}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167807 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166891 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "33f7fa4d-9ac0-552a-9f3e-9e09c2ed0286"} :step/id #uuid "2dac84d2-443e-546b-baa3-7a9ee2e2ef2c" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167808}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167808 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186168155 :tutorial/content "We can find a quadratic form's maximum and minimum values even when it contains cross-product terms. For this, we have the following theorem:\n\n*Let $A$ be the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form $Q(\\mathbf x)\\mathbin{:}$*\n\n- *The maximum value of $Q(\\mathbf{x}),$ when $\\| \\mathbf{x} \\|=1,$ is equal to the largest eigenvalue of $A{:}$* \n\n$$\n\\max \\{ Q(\\mathbf{x}) \\: | \\:  \\| \\mathbf{x} \\| = 1 \\} = \\lambda_{\\textrm{max}}\n$$\n\n*The maximum is attained on the corresponding unit eigenvector $\\mathbf{u}_{\\textrm{max}}.$ *\n\n- *The minimum value of $Q(\\mathbf{x}),$ when $\\| \\mathbf{x} \\|=1,$ is equal to the smallest eigenvalue of $A{:}$* \n\n$$\n\\min \\{ Q(\\mathbf{x}) \\: | \\:  \\| \\mathbf{x} \\| = 1 \\} = \\lambda_{\\textrm{min}}\n$$\n\n*The minimum is attained on the corresponding unit eigenvector $\\mathbf{u}_{\\textrm{min}}.$ *\n\nSuppose we are given the quadratic form \n\n$$\nQ(\\mathbf{x})=4x_1^2-2x_1x_2+4x_2^2.\n$$\n\nHow can we find a unit vector $\\mathbf{u}_{\\textrm{max}}$ at which the maximum of $Q(\\mathbf{x})$ is attained?\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix of our quadratic form:\n\n![](images/0a/0af81fbf910d2f2bbe2ad26f297f57ce230548e13ad27c2974109066b9faaee5.svg)\n\nNow, we need to calculate the eigenvalues of the matrix $A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}4-\\lambda  & -1 \\\\ -1 & 4-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )-1 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-8\\lambda +15 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -5)(\\lambda -3) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =5,\\,3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\max \\{ Q(\\mathbf{x}) \\: | \\: \\| \\mathbf{x} \\|=1 \\} = \\lambda_{\\textrm{max}} = 5.\n$$\n\nTo find $\\mathbf{u}_{\\textrm{max}},$ we need a unit eigenvector that corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda_{\\textrm{max}}=5.$ We start by computing $(A-5I)\\mathbin{:}$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-5I & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}-5\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSeeking a non-zero solution of $(A-5I)\\mathbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}$ gives the eigenvector ![](images/a2/a257df47b352c5534608079419a337ae51103dd7c7763fb73f4fd692f36fd47e.svg)\n\nFinally, dividing $\\mathbf{v}$ by its norm $\\| \\mathbf{v} \\| = \\sqrt{2},$ we get\n\n![](images/cb/cb08ba808e7b6d8a8412df8cafaa85e795f523b63450d8f4e1c3081740a46866.svg)" :tutorial/id #uuid "10db6c75-237c-5a28-b5a8-ac25c57cc82f" :tutorial/math-academy-id 7953 :tutorial/title "Constrained Optimization of Quadratic Forms"} :step/id #uuid "3892412b-7fe5-5337-9881-d9cb02031080" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167809}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167809 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166892 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3b2e9ac0-590b-587c-b16d-309f899c21e6"} :step/id #uuid "3eb3250a-641e-50c7-85ee-a4a11b6073b7"}] :activity/title 