p/id #uuid "46e11e28-122a-5f86-8bf2-7977b37760ca" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531708}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531690 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269171 :question/id #uuid "e90ca9ef-a872-5eac-99c1-91a2d454f0ae"} :step/id #uuid "66cbd984-34bf-5c4b-b040-16117bac09ca" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531663}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531708 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531584 :question/id #uuid "3e4f6268-3e58-5684-9bea-f874fd53aaf3"} :step/id #uuid "b523e58a-cade-5384-8700-ade4a5ce4089" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531690}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531718 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531621 :question/id #uuid "957651b3-45e4-5a93-853b-1785322d0942"} :step/id #uuid "d6103cc5-4c4e-5c0f-af10-d73cba662696" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531686}}] :activity/title "Constrained Optimization of Quadratic Forms" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530860}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186050447 :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166890 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166491 :question/id #uuid "b8306278-726a-5c09-86cc-14631a6abb66" :question/math-academy-id "e-12659" :question/problem "Find the maximum value of $Q(\\mathbf{x})=2x_1^2 - 5x_2^2 +3x_3^2$ given that $\\| \\mathbf{x} \\| =1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $x_1^2 \\geq 0$ and $x_2^2 \\geq 0.$ So, we have that \n\n$$\n2x_1^2 \\leq 3x_1^2, \\qquad -5x_2^2 \\leq 3x_2^2.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-5{x}_{2}^{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & \\le 3{x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =3({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $\\| \\mathbf{x} \\| = 1$ is equivalent to $x_1^2 + x_2^2 + x_3^2 =1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2})=3(1)=3,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(\\mathbf{x}) \\leq 3.$\n\nSo, the value of $Q(\\mathbf{x})$ can be no greater than $3.$ But before we conclude that $3$ is the maximum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(\\mathbf{x}) = 3.$\n\nNotice that when ![](images/c4/c4afaf37dc0b68f09e5efac6434f3f22bc8edc107f45ce7f3327c475f4158ea7.svg) we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-5{x}_{2}^{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =2(0)^{2}-5(0)^{2}+3(1)^{2} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that $\\| \\mathbf{x} \\| =1,$ the maximum value of $Q(\\mathbf{x})$ is equal to $3.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a8666dd9-b763-589d-8ae3-af203068f1a4" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167097 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ce429b82-d5fe-5135-aa2f-7549506d0a88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163661} {:answer/id #uuid "da68ef93-306d-59f0-bf29-ebe7d561723d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163662} {:answer/id #uuid "3a0d2ee0-684d-5f03-a17e-0c2b024a2261" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163663} {:answer/id #uuid "5431ee00-9f5c-5e39-962b-0e4f34bf8d82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163664} {:answer/id #uuid "7a99f312-afd8-5fed-b0ee-9b87bd394b90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163665}] :answer-field/id #uuid "0c7b774c-bbbc-5500-8a02-0d246b76d689" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163660}] :question/id #uuid "ac0817ef-b7f9-5541-b773-05ed1543f2a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-136823" :question/problem "Find the maximum value of $Q(x) = 5x_{1}^{2} + 3x_{2}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖ = 1$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167102 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9516beb9-455a-5cc4-acd9-2f4aab580daf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163691} {:answer/id #uuid "c776ec1f-1f89-5eeb-a6a6-cd6e0d0b73bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163692} {:answer/id #uuid "d4320d75-9d5d-55be-92cd-dd228b2b92d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163693} {:answer/id #uuid "4cc2b2ca-b114-5175-bbf3-2a0a05281d23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163694} {:answer/id #uuid "55147a9e-8df5-5ec2-8af3-14a446fc7cd7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163695}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163694} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f9417e7-ccc2-5461-bbb5-dcd957763f91" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186163690}] :question/id #uuid "104289cf-8277-54fc-85de-4e1b2c51d42a" :question/math-academy-id "q-138024" :question/problem "Find the maximum value of $Q(x)=4{x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that ${x}_{2}^{2}\\ge 0$ and ${x}_{3}^{2}\\ge 0.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n3{x}_{2}^{2}\\le 4{x}_{2}^{2},\\,2{x}_{3}^{2}\\le 4{x}_{3}^{2}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =4{x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & \\le 4{x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{2}^{2}+4{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =4({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $‖x‖=1$ is equivalent to ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}=1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2})=4(1)=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(x)\\le 4.$ \n\nSo, the value of $Q(x)$ can be no greater than $4.$ But before we conclude that $4$ is the maximum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(x)=4.$\n\nNotice that when $x={\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}^{T},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =4{x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =4(1)^{2}+3(0)^{2}+2(0)^{2} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that $‖x‖=1,$ the maximum value of  $Q(x)$ is equal to $4.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269159 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "091534f4-2b9c-51ca-b4ab-185a907427b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266227} {:answer/id #uuid "9562e6f4-9744-5777-bc7b-96c29764c844" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267478} {:answer/id #uuid "9f888ce2-8e3f-5c11-8ef5-456e600aadcb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267586} {:answer/id #uuid "b707f2ec-ecd1-50f2-8644-bb01a79d33e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267782} {:answer/id #uuid "c371527a-fe3b-58fc-aab7-b20e0e8fec92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267888}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267782} :answer-field/id #uuid "88013ee1-3bcc-5d3e-a9ee-6c76907a4c36" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268647}] :question/id #uuid "63de7419-e75c-59e3-b8fc-e56c9267f133" :question/math-academy-id "q-138018" :question/problem "Find the maximum value of $Q(x)=4{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that ${x}_{2}^{2}\\ge 0.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n2{x}_{2}^{2}\\le 4{x}_{2}^{2}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =4{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & \\le 4{x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =4({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $‖x‖=1$ is equivalent to ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}=1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2})=4(1)=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(x)\\le 4.$\n\nSo, the value of $Q(x)$ can be no greater than $4.$ But before we conclude that $4$ is the maximum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(x)=4.$\n\nNotice that when  $x={\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}^{T},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =4{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =4(1)^{2}+2(0)^{2} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that $‖x‖=1,$ the maximum value of $Q(x)$ is equal to $4.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269160 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d6f64ea-5883-59b6-87d8-0c414835bf9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266397} {:answer/id #uuid "64bf79c6-9bd3-58b2-a03f-31ea6d676ad2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267035} {:answer/id #uuid "6835f060-12f4-5f7c-800f-2d11804b0999" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267068} {:answer/id #uuid "75d606cc-7006-5c54-8b0d-87575a052797" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267183} {:answer/id #uuid "8b01eb48-f505-5230-9bfc-e142c70b0dcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267391}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267391} :answer-field/id #uuid "28c921d2-404f-547b-a4f2-1796fd2b6c1d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268470}] :question/id #uuid "4b3d9103-b2fd-58c5-b20f-fd57d948503c" :question/math-academy-id "q-138021" :question/problem "Find the maximum value of $Q(x)=2{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{2}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that ${x}_{2}^{2}\\ge 0.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n-4{x}_{2}^{2}\\le 2{x}_{2}^{2}.\n$$\n\nAs a result,  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & \\le 2{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $‖x‖=1$ is equivalent to ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}=1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2})=2(1)=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(x)\\le 2.$\n\nSo, the value of $Q(x)$ can be no greater than $2.$ But before we conclude that $2$ is the maximum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(x)=2.$\n\nNotice that when $x={\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}^{T},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2(1)^{2}-4(0)^{2} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, given that $‖x‖=1,$ the maximum value of $Q(x)$ is equal to $2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269161 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a2b5512-df42-581a-b353-3fabc43cee3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266235} {:answer/id #uuid "97b2abc9-31d1-5823-9bc4-76f1d7b7e754" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267501} {:answer/id #uuid "9d61cd04-19aa-52dd-b6e1-03d9829033b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267560} {:answer/id #uuid "a1f07942-a1d9-5001-83ad-0233540581f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267600} {:answer/id #uuid "df0b9433-e3c9-59d0-a9f8-afcc07ddf9d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268115}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267560} :answer-field/id #uuid "73d457e3-1350-5f7d-95f8-cb4b91e459e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268622}] :question/id #uuid "af1b3d3b-8379-544e-8bfe-948c68812b5f" :question/math-academy-id "q-138023" :question/problem "Find the maximum value of $Q(x)=2{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}-3{x}_{3}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that ${x}_{3}^{2}\\ge 0.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n-3{x}_{3}^{2}\\le 2{x}_{3}^{2}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}-3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & \\le 2{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =2({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $‖x‖=1$ is equivalent to ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}=1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2})=2(1)=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(x)\\le 2.$\n\nSo, the value of $Q(x)$ can be no greater than $2.$ But before we conclude that $2$ is the maximum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(x)=2.$\n\nNotice that when $x={\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}^{T},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}-3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =2(0)^{2}+2(1)^{2}-3(0)^{2} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that $‖x‖=1,$ the maximum value of $Q(x)$ is equal to $2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278196 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "046e5cff-9e1c-5464-8f14-10687540d97b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275517} {:answer/id #uuid "0f847152-42ba-54a6-a8c1-bed65cf52949" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275610} {:answer/id #uuid "2e12f887-2b42-5ff8-a59a-f5a0a911afa1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275893} {:answer/id #uuid "42d11b76-5166-552d-9ab9-c864833027ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276066} {:answer/id #uuid "5d46f792-6bb7-5c98-a838-c508642a093a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276309}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275893} :answer-field/id #uuid "611db0db-e4e0-5fc8-9899-907fb360d2dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277897}] :question/id #uuid "3ba0d5a0-909a-5afd-930c-63e0cd27ecd8" :question/math-academy-id "q-158468" :question/problem "Find the maximum value of $Q(x)=5{x}_{1}^{2}+8{x}_{2}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that ${x}_{1}^{2}\\ge 0.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n5{x}_{1}^{2}\\le 8{x}_{1}^{2}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =5{x}_{1}^{2}+8{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & \\le 8{x}_{1}^{2}+8{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =8({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $‖x‖=1$ is equivalent to ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}=1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2})=8(1)=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(x)\\le 8.$\n\nSo, the value of $Q(x)$ can be no greater than $8.$ But before we conclude that $8$ is the maximum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(x)=8.$\n\nNotice that when  $x={\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{T},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =5{x}_{1}^{2}+8{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =5(0)^{2}+8(1)^{2} \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that $‖x‖=1,$ the maximum value of $Q(x)$ is equal to $8.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278197 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0038ddda-e455-5e22-b133-45f5afd6bfa8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275481} {:answer/id #uuid "4c6fe5fb-e999-5dc9-a386-3749054aca39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276151} {:answer/id #uuid "7ad233a9-13ef-5aca-a1bd-8edf1a1dd256" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276591} {:answer/id #uuid "926a1bae-a807-5bfe-b855-f0f51c9d9e7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276801} {:answer/id #uuid "e7e28dbb-2254-50d6-bde2-6c9cabe1d0bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277506}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275481} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b630154-06fe-530e-bfba-fa83ff574f2b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277845}] :question/id #uuid "e74167c4-c7fe-5e65-910c-e5deae2cc1bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-158526" :question/problem "Find the maximum value of $Q(x)=2{x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2}-5{x}_{3}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that ${x}_{2}^{2}\\ge 0$ and ${x}_{3}^{2}\\ge 0.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n-3{x}_{2}^{2}\\le 2{x}_{2}^{2},\\,-5{x}_{3}^{2}\\le 2{x}_{3}^{2}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2}-5{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & \\le 2{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =2({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $‖x‖=1$ is equivalent to ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}=1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2})=2(1)=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(x)\\le 2.$\n\nSo, the value of $Q(x)$ can be no greater than $2.$ But before we conclude that $2$ is the maximum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(x)=2.$\n\nNotice that when $x={\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}^{T},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2}-5{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =2(1)^{2}-3(0)^{2}-5(0)^{2} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that $‖x‖=1,$ the maximum value of $Q(x)$ is equal to $2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278198 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14498f09-4697-5338-a323-cc4fa83f67ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275666} {:answer/id #uuid "c7f8839c-9d93-526f-89cc-6f8351fc9042" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277254} {:answer/id #uuid "e4357fc2-6186-5ce0-b741-7d5068a8d399" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277468} {:answer/id #uuid "ecc5e1a1-3ce8-5582-a69a-dd6d2ba8d8a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277552} {:answer/id #uuid "f620235a-628a-5b8b-9407-f0ac5946e970" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277632}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277552} :answer-field/id #uuid "872e74bf-5759-5c92-88cb-a75ba5be6892" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277968}] :question/id #uuid "e7e7954d-9da2-5615-9bcc-af43d080c381" :question/math-academy-id "q-158528" :question/problem "Find the maximum value of $Q(x)=2{x}_{1}^{2}-7{x}_{2}^{2}+4{x}_{3}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that ${x}_{1}^{2}\\ge 0$ and ${x}_{2}^{2}\\ge 0.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n2{x}_{1}^{2}\\le 4{x}_{1}^{2},\\,-7{x}_{2}^{2}\\le 4{x}_{2}^{2}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-7{x}_{2}^{2}+4{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & \\le 4{x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{2}^{2}+4{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =4({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $‖x‖=1$ is equivalent to ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}=1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2})=4(1)=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(x)\\le 4.$\n\nSo, the value of $Q(x)$ can be no greater than $4.$ But before we conclude that $4$ is the maximum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(x)=4.$\n\nNotice that when $x={\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{T},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-7{x}_{2}^{2}+4{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =2(0)^{2}-7(0)^{2}+4(1)^{2} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that $‖x‖=1,$ the maximum value of $Q(x)$ is equal to $4.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378759 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c051e1e-9e72-5d6d-82b8-f28b68533602" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378761} {:answer/id #uuid "af95651a-de2f-555f-ae3c-e83ff3491dfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378762} {:answer/id #uuid "c8108d8b-bcce-577a-994e-6f67d119c1c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378763} {:answer/id #uuid "71e06af8-fa30-564b-8609-7dd83e64cbcb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378764} {:answer/id #uuid "10bfe917-e56f-5915-a08d-592cd912ac79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378765}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378763} :answer-field/id #uuid "69041f32-949e-5bd8-9f4b-53eadb70896e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378760}] :question/id #uuid "639b5fe1-808a-5fa4-9b00-50f2df78b358" :question/math-academy-id "q-158527" :question/problem "Find the maximum value of $Q(x)=3{x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{2}^{2}+4{x}_{3}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that ${x}_{1}^{2}\\ge 0$ and ${x}_{3}^{2}\\ge 0.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n3{x}_{1}^{2}\\le 6{x}_{1}^{2},\\,4{x}_{3}^{2}\\le 6{x}_{3}^{2}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =3{x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{2}^{2}+4{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & \\le 6{x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{2}^{2}+6{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =6({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $‖x‖=1$ is equivalent to ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}=1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2})=6(1)=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(x)\\le 6.$ \n\nSo, the value of $Q(x)$ can be no greater than $6.$ But before we conclude that $6$ is the maximum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(x)=6.$\n\nNotice that when $x={\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}^{T},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =3{x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{2}^{2}+4{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =3(0)^{2}+6(1)^{2}+4(0)^{2} \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that $‖x‖=1,$ the maximum value of  $Q(x)$ is equal to $6.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186531621 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "216c258d-237e-56bc-84d0-723783afd364" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186530936} {:answer/id #uuid "5f0626f9-e9e4-50c5-b013-a1beded68ff5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531074} {:answer/id #uuid "7cc3c5b6-4c5a-5c36-a2ed-e4ddbb6fc109" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531138} {:answer/id #uuid "c5f228cb-9e36-5dd9-b182-62125ce92bee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531277} {:answer/id #uuid "c8ebcb55-7a36-5694-83c4-9fdbd78afeec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531283}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531138} :answer-field/id #uuid "90167cb7-250b-5746-b04f-a31c7f3561cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186531481}] :question/id #uuid "957651b3-45e4-5a93-853b-1785322d0942" :question/math-academy-id "q-138022" :question/problem "Find the maximum value of $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that ${x}_{2}^{2}\\ge 0.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n-{x}_{2}^{2}\\le {x}_{2}^{2}.\n$$\n\nAs a result,  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & \\le {x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $‖x‖=1$ is equivalent to ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}=1.$ So,  in turn, $Q(x)\\le 1.$\n\nSo, the value of $Q(x)$ can be no greater than $1.$ But before we conclude that $1$ is the maximum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(x)=1.$\n\nNotice that when $x={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =(1)^{2}-(0)^{2} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, given that $‖x‖=1,$ the maximum value of $Q(x)$ is equal to $1.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Maximum Value Given a Canonical Form on the Unit Sphere"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166891 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166492 :question/id #uuid "5b4117f3-62fb-55c6-8e23-0cadcd4a2ec5" :question/math-academy-id "e-12660" :question/problem "Find the minimum value of $Q(\\mathbf{x})=5x_1^2 - 4x_2^2 - 6x_3^2$ given that $\\| \\mathbf{x} \\| =1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $x_1^2 \\geq 0$ and $x_2^2 \\geq 0.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n5x_1^2 \\geq -6x_1^2, \\qquad -4x_2^2 \\geq -6x_2^2.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =5{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{2}^{2}-6{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & \\ge -6{x}_{1}^{2}-6{x}_{2}^{2}-6{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =-6({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $\\| \\mathbf{x} \\| = 1$ is equivalent to $x_1^2 + x_2^2 + x_3^2 =1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2})=-6(1)=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(\\mathbf{x}) \\geq -6.$\n\nSo, the value of $Q(\\mathbf{x})$ can be no smaller than $-6.$ But before we conclude that $-6$ is the minimum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(\\mathbf{x}) = -6.$\n\nNotice that when ![](images/cf/cfee6f101db09d50c60a1f539ebb116e5b3912ac0dfc1ee3fb646ecf7f3f6287.svg) we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =5{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{2}^{2}-6{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =5(0)^{2}-4(0)^{2}-6(1)^{2} \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that $\\| \\mathbf{x} \\| =1,$ the minimum value of $Q(\\mathbf{x})$ is equal to $-6.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "33f7fa4d-9ac0-552a-9f3e-9e09c2ed0286" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167098 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46924927-06ec-56cb-98e1-4a9f8257bf59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266774} {:answer/id #uuid "8a6af117-5920-5cc7-ba0d-0d5bb48ed086" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267379} {:answer/id #uuid "a80d8439-2c6f-5e40-a229-93b535ff35b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267665} {:answer/id #uuid "f03bd214-43d7-5b50-bb06-16406a90f3a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268281} {:answer/id #uuid "f0d9261b-1e2a-5411-931c-6dd0970c4046" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268286}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266774} :answer-field/id #uuid "89fbe449-3952-54bf-9b43-6ba33b308a80" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268652}] :question/id #uuid "0706b1eb-0c66-56aa-86af-d962b1e95896" :question/math-academy-id "q-136824" :question/problem "Find the minimum value of $Q(x)=2{x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{3}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that ${x}_{1}^{2}\\ge 0$ and ${x}_{3}^{2}\\ge 0.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n2{x}_{1}^{2}\\ge -3{x}_{1}^{2},\\,-{x}_{3}^{2}\\ge -3{x}_{3}^{2}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & \\ge -3{x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2}-3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =-3({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $‖x‖=1$ is equivalent to ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}=1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2})=-3(1)=-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(x)\\ge -3.$\n\nSo, the value of $Q(x)$ can be no smaller than $-3.$ But before we conclude that $-3$ is the minimum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(x)=-3.$\n\nNotice that when $x={\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}^{T},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =2(0)^{2}-3(1)^{2}-(0)^{2} \\\\  & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that $‖x‖=1,$ the minimum value of $Q(x)$ is equal to $-3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167101 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bb2b3ec-b506-57b1-a321-ef34d500b312" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266380} {:answer/id #uuid "3fb34a44-ccc4-5d93-a0ee-d1a270a49f96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266719} {:answer/id #uuid "7ce773be-46a8-5749-9f3c-45e0184f84dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267250} {:answer/id #uuid "950803c3-f359-5b8b-854f-fac51f406e73" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267475} {:answer/id #uuid "a9a6f32c-3450-50b7-a94c-f53570e5d4d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267675}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266380} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fae4afb-886b-5f96-b0c8-2b5e66121cf1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268513}] :question/id #uuid "657b8539-11db-5516-89dc-20b2cb407f63" :question/math-academy-id "q-138019" :question/problem "Find the minimum value of $Q(x)=5{x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that ${x}_{1}^{2}\\ge 0.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n5{x}_{1}^{2}\\ge 3{x}_{1}^{2}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =5{x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & \\ge 3{x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =3({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $‖x‖=1$ is equivalent to ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}=1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2})=3(1)=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(x)\\ge 3.$ \n\nSo, the value of $Q(x)$ can be no smaller than $3.$ But before we conclude that $3$ is the minimum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(x)=3.$\n\nNotice that when  $x={\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{T},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =5{x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =5(0)+3(1)^{2} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that $‖x‖=1,$ the minimum value of $Q(x)$ is equal to $3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269162 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "426b242e-82e1-5cb1-8e9a-c5f3406c7b6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266737} {:answer/id #uuid "a698ddc5-e273-545c-92f3-c9e3a7a2206e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267651} {:answer/id #uuid "af666caa-2f0b-52bd-b6ae-306a82069c11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267723} {:answer/id #uuid "e8263730-14a1-5854-bc66-a40ac358112e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268202} {:answer/id #uuid "ed865f26-135f-5470-92f3-701998ca3801" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268254}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266737} :answer-field/id #uuid "5cae1c8d-1f0a-50b4-af56-974bf2368c7b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268573}] :question/id #uuid "c5b94d26-7531-5fec-94da-00c9ed7c30a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-138029" :question/problem "Find the minimum value of $Q(x)=4{x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that ${x}_{1}^{2}\\ge 0$ and ${x}_{3}^{2}\\ge 0.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n4{x}_{1}^{2}\\ge 2{x}_{1}^{2},\\,3{x}_{2}^{2}\\ge 2{x}_{2}^{2}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =4{x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & \\ge 2{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =2({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $‖x‖=1$ is equivalent to ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}=1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2})=2(1)=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(x)\\ge 2.$\n\nSo, the value of $Q(x)$ can be no smaller than $2.$ But before we conclude that $2$ is the minimum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(x)=2.$\n\nNotice that when  $x={\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{T},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =4{x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =4(0)^{2}+3(0)^{2}+2(1)^{2} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that $‖x‖=1,$ the minimum value of $Q(x)$ is equal to $2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269164 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fddd54e-2f69-5317-9273-59acf0420171" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266424} {:answer/id #uuid "488b4f03-ec81-5e5e-88ac-1e1b03de77fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266792} {:answer/id #uuid "6c2ad35c-a214-5c83-bfd9-e7a6a53c9023" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267099} {:answer/id #uuid "c18a481a-15ba-5133-9b96-62027df826c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267872} {:answer/id #uuid "ff581e6d-531a-50a8-93f1-45b62be1bbc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268394}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267872} :answer-field/id #uuid "a2163251-a2b2-5338-af76-79765630ea17" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268695}] :question/id #uuid "d2bb923d-a428-53a1-96e5-4cae59c3d2d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-138064" :question/problem "Find the minimum value of $Q(x)=4{x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{3}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that ${x}_{1}^{2}\\ge 0$ and ${x}_{2}^{2}\\ge 0.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n4{x}_{1}^{2}\\ge -2{x}_{1}^{2},\\,-{x}_{2}^{2}\\ge -2{x}_{2}^{2}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =4{x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & \\ge -2{x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =-2({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $‖x‖=1$ is equivalent to ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}=1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2})=-2(1)=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(x)\\ge -2.$ \n\nSo, the value of $Q(x)$ can be no smaller than $-2.$ But before we conclude that $-2$ is the minimum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(x)=-2.$\n\nNotice that when $x={\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{T},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =4{x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =4(0)^{2}-(0)^{2}-2(1)^{2} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that $‖x‖=1,$ the minimum value of $Q(x)$ is equal to $-2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269165 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "153b1cc1-f1b8-5692-a555-aa83d2319c1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266324} {:answer/id #uuid "1ad4911c-bca4-53c3-a9c7-19d389a73796" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266371} {:answer/id #uuid "5633496f-0847-5ac2-8354-19bbb38416c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266912} {:answer/id #uuid "f6b02623-7d38-5701-b7a5-be9d5aecb396" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268330} {:answer/id #uuid "f8b14a00-455b-5248-9a67-9f02bd5571df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268348}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266324} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6a67f1a-a4d6-5410-a486-f5c067d11840" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268839}] :question/id #uuid "12200f9b-72b6-5817-8209-f85aa2b1e6f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-138065" :question/problem "Find the minimum value of $Q(x)=-3{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{2}^{2}+5{x}_{3}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that ${x}_{1}^{2}\\ge 0$ and ${x}_{3}^{2}\\ge 0.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n-3{x}_{1}^{2}\\ge -4{x}_{1}^{2},\\,5{x}_{3}^{2}\\ge -4{x}_{3}^{2}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =-3{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{2}^{2}+5{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & \\ge -4{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{2}^{2}-4{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =-4({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $‖x‖=1$ is equivalent to ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}=1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2})=-4(1)=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(x)\\ge -4.$   \n\nSo, the value of $Q(x)$ can be no smaller than $-4.$ But before we conclude that $-4$ is the minimum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(x)=-4.$\n\nNotice that when $x={\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}^{T},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =-3{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{2}^{2}+5{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =-3(0)^{2}-4(1)^{2}+5(0)^{2} \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that $‖x‖=1,$ the minimum value of $Q(x)$ is equal to $-4.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278199 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09b79818-ec47-55bc-b609-63c6c7f161ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275560} {:answer/id #uuid "323fcb23-e5ea-5a1e-bc6b-e65f4146ffd7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275920} {:answer/id #uuid "729259e1-80fc-5388-9d30-d99ee12044d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276514} {:answer/id #uuid "7da4754f-dbb6-521e-9c6c-fe4033a96679" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276621} {:answer/id #uuid "fe5b7457-be1f-5d50-8ded-808417ee142a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277709}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275560} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c00b02e-46dc-5d0c-b7da-153ae5f706cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277747}] :question/id #uuid "e1c124bc-a836-51e9-a514-6920747fc0ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-158529" :question/problem "Find the minimum value of $Q(x)=-4{x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that ${x}_{2}^{2}\\ge 0.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n-3{x}_{2}^{2}\\ge -4{x}_{2}^{2}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =-4{x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & \\ge -4{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =-4({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $‖x‖=1$ is equivalent to ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}=1.$ So,  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2})=-4(1)=-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(x)\\ge -4.$\n\nSo, the value of $Q(x)$ can be no smaller than $-4.$ But before we conclude that $-4$ is the minimum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(x)=-4.$\n\nNotice that when $x={\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}^{T},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =-4{x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =-4(1)^{2}-3(0)^{2} \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that $‖x‖=1,$ the minimum value of $Q(x)$ is equal to $-4.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278200 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "018c99a3-0395-5f65-a414-0b527b9b1fb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275490} {:answer/id #uuid "2418fd71-994a-57d9-8058-e7d13fe938ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275795} {:answer/id #uuid "724c24fe-2a6a-593e-84fa-821ecbbea055" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276512} {:answer/id #uuid "adf63806-8714-5759-974a-7ebb5953e7da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277040} {:answer/id #uuid "c1115abc-a234-5591-8bd4-08bbcb550a6c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277193}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275795} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5356da2-3693-5794-9588-7fc99e91ebda" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278045}] :question/id #uuid "7a98e5a2-f222-532b-be08-4de02d1187ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-158533" :question/problem "Find the minimum value of $Q(x)=3{x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{2}^{2}+4{x}_{3}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that ${x}_{2}^{2}\\ge 0$ and ${x}_{3}^{2}\\ge 0.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n6{x}_{2}^{2}\\ge 3{x}_{2}^{2},\\,4{x}_{3}^{2}\\ge 3{x}_{3}^{2}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =3{x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{2}^{2}+4{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & \\ge 3{x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =3({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $‖x‖=1$ is equivalent to ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}=1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2})=3(1)=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(x)\\ge 3.$\n\nSo, the value of $Q(x)$ can be no smaller than $3.$ But before we conclude that $3$ is the minimum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(x)=3.$\n\nNotice that when  $x={\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}^{T},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =3{x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{2}^{2}+4{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =3(1)^{2}+6(0)^{2}+4(0)^{2} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that $‖x‖=1,$ the minimum value of $Q(x)$ is equal to $3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378691 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9217c64c-f4ce-5bae-87a0-2ea2943f0b28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378693} {:answer/id #uuid "4cf0cecc-df02-5cc0-95f2-b2284b53af6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378694} {:answer/id #uuid "b7b98e55-1729-5042-9ce3-6892bb7ccf75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378695} {:answer/id #uuid "071c1f48-d600-5a24-ad0d-0ac4cc840fcb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378696} {:answer/id #uuid "393fd00f-0785-5b3b-a908-8533f2c414c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378697}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378697} :answer-field/id #uuid "2bd4ef65-6095-5c31-aec9-f72c5da78e6d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378692}] :question/id #uuid "708c581a-e4d5-52e1-b94e-b31cc7a9545c" :question/math-academy-id "q-138020" :question/problem "Find the minimum value of $Q(x)=3{x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that ${x}_{1}^{2}\\ge 0.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n3{x}_{1}^{2}\\ge -2{x}_{1}^{2}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =3{x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & \\ge -2{x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =-2({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $‖x‖=1$ is equivalent to ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}=1.$ So,  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2})=-2(1)=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(x)\\ge -2.$\n\nSo, the value of $Q(x)$ can be no smaller than $-2.$ But before we conclude that $-2$ is the minimum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(x)=-2.$\n\nNotice that when $x={\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{T},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =3{x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =3(0)^{2}-2(1)^{2} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that $‖x‖=1,$ the minimum value of $Q(x)$ is equal to $-2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378766 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30b8156c-9e64-5b61-aeca-3d74ab19e687" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378768} {:answer/id #uuid "1202061a-84a4-5c46-9aa8-4d93661b1821" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378769} {:answer/id #uuid "c245ed11-7e16-5fa9-ae7e-f4e114301629" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378770} {:answer/id #uuid "8a47f02d-1175-5723-a197-e394ca432c8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378771} {:answer/id #uuid "0ced1311-6372-5c20-b9d4-b10fbcd2aba4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378772}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378772} :answer-field/id #uuid "33e74247-61c0-5aec-9e37-8a7504fd27bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378767}] :question/id #uuid "1c3dbcd3-9baa-5224-bea6-485712c20c3b" :question/math-academy-id "q-158532" :question/problem "Find the minimum value of $Q(x)=4{x}_{1}^{2}-6{x}_{2}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that ${x}_{1}^{2}\\ge 0.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n4{x}_{1}^{2}\\ge -6{x}_{1}^{2}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =4{x}_{1}^{2}-6{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & \\ge -6{x}_{1}^{2}-6{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =-6({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $‖x‖=1$ is equivalent to ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}=1.$ So,  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2})=-6(1)=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(x)\\ge -6.$\n\nSo, the value of $Q(x)$ can be no smaller than $-6.$ But before we conclude that $-6$ is the minimum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(x)=-6.$\n\nNotice that when $x={\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{T},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =4{x}_{1}^{2}-6{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =4(0)^{2}-6(1)^{2} \\\\  & =-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that $‖x‖=1,$ the minimum value of $Q(x)$ is equal to $-6.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492028 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7af27e76-63ba-50ec-8eb2-b883774e51ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491669} {:answer/id #uuid "7b2ba24e-ff58-5939-98b8-c0a4ae606ce5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491671} {:answer/id #uuid "89eb46f6-972b-5dce-a398-209e4aac862e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491689} {:answer/id #uuid "d3b19c16-3291-5a56-87dc-4937a4b60eb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491814} {:answer/id #uuid "f4486f88-56ea-5beb-bb11-91eb5a7aa4e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491871}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491669} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed2b6ea2-7bc6-53de-a437-5cb53c04fb85" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491977}] :question/id #uuid "77d3128f-57d6-56c8-a326-3ba5851a500a" :question/math-academy-id "q-158530" :question/problem "Find the minimum value of $Q(x)=-2{x}_{1}^{2}-5{x}_{2}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that ${x}_{1}^{2}\\ge 0.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n-2{x}_{1}^{2}\\ge -5{x}_{1}^{2}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =-2{x}_{1}^{2}-5{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & \\ge -5{x}_{1}^{2}-5{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =-5({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $‖x‖=1$ is equivalent to ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}=1.$ So,  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2})=-5(1)=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(x)\\ge -5.$\n\nSo, the value of $Q(x)$ can be no smaller than $-5.$ But before we conclude that $-5$ is the minimum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(x)=-5.$\n\nNotice that when $x={\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{T},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =-2{x}_{1}^{2}-5{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =-2(0)^{2}-5(1)^{2} \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that $‖x‖=1,$ the minimum value of $Q(x)$ is equal to $-5.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186492073 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1eb4aba8-ac20-5cbd-be43-99fed3db4846" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491519} {:answer/id #uuid "2c883ac6-45f3-5671-8996-be49b1f4a1fb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491544} {:answer/id #uuid "68330fbe-d8f3-5d83-9652-1a55a837aea6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491641} {:answer/id #uuid "8c90b13a-d0a3-5b8a-8698-21fda41d9626" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491693} {:answer/id #uuid "a57f100c-02ec-5d7d-9c50-3f1638cc0828" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491741}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491693} :answer-field/id #uuid "704abb49-2936-53d0-b0de-fa6cfab24dbc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186491925}] :question/id #uuid "fce93d41-81b4-5cb3-80dd-626cc0b50873" :question/math-academy-id "q-158535" :question/problem "Find the minimum value of $Q(x)=-5{x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that ${x}_{2}^{2}\\ge 0$ and ${x}_{3}^{2}\\ge 0.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n-3{x}_{2}^{2}\\ge -5{x}_{2}^{2},\\,2{x}_{3}^{2}\\ge -5{x}_{3}^{2}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =-5{x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & \\ge -5{x}_{1}^{2}-5{x}_{2}^{2}-5{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =-5({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $‖x‖=1$ is equivalent to ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}=1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-5({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2})=-5(1)=-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(x)\\ge -5.$   \n\nSo, the value of $Q(x)$ can be no smaller than $-5.$ But before we conclude that $-5$ is the minimum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(x)=-5.$\n\nNotice that when $x={\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}^{T},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =-5{x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =-5(1)^{2}-3(0)^{2}+2(0)^{2} \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that $‖x‖=1,$ the minimum value of $Q(x)$ is equal to $-5.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186503749 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "48ff6dc6-4553-5e13-910b-8df5f5a3bb78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503117} {:answer/id #uuid "4b434ef3-0980-5783-ad7e-eefe4f77ca09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503121} {:answer/id #uuid "55b888f5-b538-5f15-a7af-99357234caef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503146} {:answer/id #uuid "e428a7ec-4298-5c6e-9db5-e04a6ff4716f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503447} {:answer/id #uuid "e5d57557-c662-5e95-a738-e083bf15044c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503452}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503121} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb2b65ea-ec2e-55f1-a3f9-78f34b463133" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503617}] :question/id #uuid "df4de458-1c06-5aa0-8cdd-76f4342f8dfd" :question/math-academy-id "q-158531" :question/problem "Find the minimum value of $Q(x)=4{x}_{1}^{2}+7{x}_{2}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that ${x}_{2}^{2}\\ge 0.$ So, we have that\n\n$$\n7{x}_{2}^{2}\\ge 4{x}_{2}^{2}.\n$$\n\nAs a result, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =4{x}_{1}^{2}+7{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & \\ge 4{x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =4({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall that $‖x‖=1$ is equivalent to ${x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}=1.$ So, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4({x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2})=4(1)=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand, in turn, $Q(x)\\ge 4.$ \n\nSo, the value of $Q(x)$ can be no smaller than $4.$ But before we conclude that $4$ is the minimum, we need to find a vector such that $Q(x)=4.$\n\nNotice that when  $x={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}^{T},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =4{x}_{1}^{2}+7{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =4(1)+7(0)^{2} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, given that $‖x‖=1,$ the minimum value of $Q(x)$ is equal to $4.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Minimum Value Given a Canonical Form on the Unit Sphere"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166892 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166493 :question/id #uuid "3cec995b-8918-5c48-927e-b0807a947518" :question/math-academy-id "e-12661" :question/problem "Find the minimum value of $Q(\\mathbf{x})=x_1^2-2x_2^2-2x_3^2+2x_2x_3$  given that $\\| \\mathbf{x} \\| = 1.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $A$ be the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form. Recall that: \n\n- The maximum value of $Q(\\mathbf{x}),$ when $\\| \\mathbf{x} \\|=1,$ is equal to the largest eigenvalue of $A{:}$\n\n$$\n\\max \\{ Q(\\mathbf{x}) \\: | \\:  \\| \\mathbf{x} \\| = 1 \\} = \\lambda_{\\textrm{max}}\n$$\n\n- The minimum value of $Q(\\mathbf{x}),$ when $\\| \\mathbf{x} \\|=1,$ is equal to the smallest eigenvalue of $A{:}$\n\n$$\n\\min \\{ Q(\\mathbf{x}) \\: | \\:  \\| \\mathbf{x} \\| = 1 \\} = \\lambda_{\\textrm{min}}\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix of our quadratic form:\n\n![](images/e2/e2f302904c9cd4126b12ef7c1839a6f4aa0f5f02fae8b1ab749bc2c2924eb584.svg)\n\nNow, we need to calculate the eigenvalues of the matrix $A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-2-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )((-2-\\lambda )(-2-\\lambda )-1) & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda +3) & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )(\\lambda +3)(\\lambda +1) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =1,\\,-1,\\,-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\min \\{ Q(\\mathbf{x}) \\: | \\:  \\| \\mathbf{x} \\| = 1 \\} = -3.\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3b2e9ac0-590b-587c-b16d-309f899c21e6" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167099 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "56933511-7bac-56df-b79c-e43f47de1424" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378686} {:answer/id #uuid "af549cc0-3f08-5b96-911b-8266acb72440" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378687} {:answer/id #uuid "1ae28847-626b-5c4b-84eb-5668493198b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378688} {:answer/id #uuid "6616269d-d8b0-5e02-b6cc-b20f0191ea43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378689} {:answer/id #uuid "4d29e524-5968-5c11-92b5-924629837ad0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378690}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378686} :answer-field/id #uuid "693f5701-baa5-5230-8d27-8fbfe6ab9c1c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378685}] :question/id #uuid "cdc523d0-2005-5617-9a5b-100488432c13" :question/math-academy-id "q-136825" :question/problem "Find the maximum value of $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $A$ be the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form. Recall that: \n\n- The maximum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the largest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmax\\{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1\\}={\\lambda }_{\\text{max}}\n$$\n\n- The minimum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the smallest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmin\\{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1\\}={\\lambda }_{\\text{min}}\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix of our quadratic form:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to calculate the eigenvalues of the matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}1-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )-4 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda -3 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +1) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =3,\\,-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nmax\\{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1\\}=3.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167100 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d57b4db-6d97-50c9-9610-473062de51c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266545} {:answer/id #uuid "381a1650-88e7-5895-92a4-54d80c6f41ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266630} {:answer/id #uuid "a43a4fd4-4cb6-534b-b19e-d93a34bf16ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267623} {:answer/id #uuid "ce902b47-557a-5a8c-88e4-f101e42dce23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267989} {:answer/id #uuid "d68c4f89-2fe1-5fa4-a817-0703ba8e0fc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268055}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268055} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a4e85e1-14c0-5a34-8b71-adb11fa6ae6a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268678}] :question/id #uuid "6524f432-8e1b-53f9-ae30-319b701fe5f0" :question/math-academy-id "q-136826" :question/problem "Find the minimum value of $Q(x)=7{x}_{1}^{2}+8{x}_{2}^{2}+5{x}_{3}^{2}-4{x}_{2}{x}_{3}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $A$ be the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form. Recall that: \n\n- The maximum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the largest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmax{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}={\\lambda }_{\\text{max}}\n$$\n\n- The minimum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the smallest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmin{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}={\\lambda }_{\\text{min}}\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix of our quadratic form:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to calculate the eigenvalues of the matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}7-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 8-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 5-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (7-\\lambda )\\begin{vmatrix}8-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ -2 & 5-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (7-\\lambda )((8-\\lambda )(5-\\lambda )-4) & =0 \\\\ (7-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda +36) & =0 \\\\ (7-\\lambda )(\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -9) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =9,\\,7,\\,4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nmin{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}=4.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269166 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32e0125b-e672-5de3-b0bf-e83001144caa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266592} {:answer/id #uuid "8a2fae57-ad45-507d-8c5c-954002d5296a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267373} {:answer/id #uuid "b99e95e1-68cc-501b-8753-06189a9b5c3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267808} {:answer/id #uuid "dd4eaaa5-fa79-518f-aaf9-393c8ce56e15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268099} {:answer/id #uuid "e8b5064a-a188-58a9-a5cc-edc293399ecd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268209}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266592} :answer-field/id #uuid "709f832b-380c-5dc3-9199-423e6cfbc1c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268614}] :question/id #uuid "8822d1a2-73e9-5933-adc5-14944ec98673" :question/math-academy-id "q-138066" :question/problem "Find the maximum value of $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+8{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $A$ be the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form. Recall that: \n\n- The maximum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the largest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmax{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}={\\lambda }_{\\text{max}}\n$$\n\n- The minimum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the smallest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmin{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}={\\lambda }_{\\text{min}}\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix of our quadratic form:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to calculate the eigenvalues of the matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}1-\\lambda  & 4 \\\\ 4 & 1-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )-16 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda -15 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +3)(\\lambda -5) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =-3,\\,5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nmax{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}=5.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269167 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01b2b2d4-4a92-5ca7-8773-585dc47545e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266158} {:answer/id #uuid "1579bd24-79ab-5ae5-855a-9e01a8e981c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266325} {:answer/id #uuid "61936403-30d9-53a2-b50b-9d5bdd921634" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267005} {:answer/id #uuid "7da1a3b0-3738-55d7-b984-bee73e145107" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267254} {:answer/id #uuid "d74a7220-a06c-5935-bafe-a64c4952b8a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268058}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267005} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cb5642c-7627-5dca-a62a-292e78327201" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268453}] :question/id #uuid "0245ff8a-62ef-503c-845b-a63c21512dda" :question/math-academy-id "q-138067" :question/problem "Find the minimum value of $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}-8{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-5{x}_{2}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $A$ be the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form. Recall that: \n\n- The maximum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the largest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmax{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}={\\lambda }_{\\text{max}}\n$$\n\n- The minimum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the smallest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmin{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}={\\lambda }_{\\text{min}}\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix of our quadratic form:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 \\\\ -4 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to calculate the eigenvalues of the matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}1-\\lambda  & -4 \\\\ -4 & -5-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )(-5-\\lambda )-16 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+4\\lambda -21 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +7) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =3,\\,-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nmin{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1}=-7.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269168 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "233cbc8c-e991-527f-9870-8237e9259827" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266464} {:answer/id #uuid "56e3fb50-941c-5071-8184-b8b5efbbc951" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266917} {:answer/id #uuid "75092e81-eb62-517d-a2e7-5d3e74d2d302" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267174} {:answer/id #uuid "86732239-f564-5d20-a6f0-287cc9127ae5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267329} {:answer/id #uuid "c2215b72-50a3-58e0-b851-56494e72a6ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267875}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267875} :answer-field/id #uuid "c559be84-8136-5eb8-a035-4f4b66f98088" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268758}] :question/id #uuid "87883ff5-3c1f-5958-9ae9-a0cb7b8aff97" :question/math-academy-id "q-138068" :question/problem "Find the maximum value of $Q(x)=5{x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+5{x}_{2}^{2}$ given that $‖x‖=1.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $A$ be the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form. Recall that: \n\n- The maximum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the largest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmax\\{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1\\}={\\lambda }_{\\text{max}}\n$$\n\n- The minimum value of $Q(x),$ when $‖x‖=1,$ is equal to the smallest eigenvalue of $A:$\n\n$$\nmin\\{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1\\}={\\lambda }_{\\text{min}}\n$$\n\nFirst, we write down the matrix of our quadratic form:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to calculate the eigenvalues of the matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|A-\\lambda I| & =0 \\\\ \\begin{vmatrix}5-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5-\\lambda \\end{vmatrix} & =0 \\\\ (5-\\lambda )(5-\\lambda )-4 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-10\\lambda +21 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -7) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =3,\\,7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nmax\\{Q(x)\\,|\\,‖x‖=1\\}=7.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269170 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04ff6694-ed52-501e-9c74-482fc606115b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266189} {:answer/id #uuid "4ac22209-68a0-5ff5-87ab-24d903edf82a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266807} {:answer/id #uuid "69d1b0b5-a3c7-5bd0-b0ea-07afbce368e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267082} {:answer/id #uuid "8ca167eb-75e4-5231-9e14-28b84b7d28c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267401} {:answer/id #uuid "8cb91b01-0006-51fd-a05f-946591dc8083" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 1759218626